00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:37.764
[soft music playing]


00:02:01.747 --> 00:02:03.749
- [birds chirping]
- [rustling]


00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:10.422
[soft music playing]


00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:15.927
[Maben] <i>It's like you wake up one day</i>


00:02:16.011 --> 00:02:17.512
<i>and you're just here...</i>


00:02:18.764 --> 00:02:21.767
<i>like a stone thrown into this world.</i>


00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.896
<i>But you don't know who threw it,</i>


00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:29.107
<i>or which direction it came from...</i>


00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:37.991
[playful howling]


00:02:48.502 --> 00:02:50.712
<i>"Go back to Mississippi," you think.</i>


00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:56.218
<i>Maybe there will be a miracle...</i>


00:02:59.054 --> 00:03:02.057
<i>some way to begin again...</i>


00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:12.317
- All right, turn this side of your head.
- No.


00:03:13.235 --> 00:03:16.029
Oh, look at how dirty that is.


00:03:16.113 --> 00:03:17.114
Mm.


00:03:18.699 --> 00:03:20.117
[Maben] <i>I wish it was true.</i>


00:03:24.413 --> 00:03:25.914
<i>God, I wish it was true.</i>


00:03:32.379 --> 00:03:33.588
[phone book rattles]


00:03:54.818 --> 00:03:56.027
[Analee] <i>Mama?</i>


00:03:56.111 --> 00:03:57.112
[Maben] <i>Yeah, baby?</i>


00:03:58.113 --> 00:04:00.073
[Analee] <i>Are we in Mississippi yet?</i>


00:04:01.116 --> 00:04:03.285
<i>Yeah, we are.</i>


00:04:03.368 --> 00:04:05.912
[Analee] <i>Can we stop walking now?</i>


00:04:05.996 --> 00:04:09.499
<i>You said once we got to Mississippi,
we could stop walking.</i>


00:04:11.793 --> 00:04:12.919
<i>Is that what I said?</i>


00:04:16.757 --> 00:04:19.384
We're gonna get a place real soon, okay?


00:04:19.468 --> 00:04:22.721
For now, you have got to go to sleep,


00:04:22.804 --> 00:04:26.933
and you better dream about
that chocolate ice cream that you had.


00:04:30.729 --> 00:04:32.397
- Mama?
- Yeah.


00:04:32.481 --> 00:04:34.733
Tell about Mississippi again.


00:04:36.818 --> 00:04:38.403
Mm... okay.


00:04:39.905 --> 00:04:40.822
Well...


00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.076
[sniffs] Mississippi...


00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:47.370
was your daddy's favorite place.


00:04:47.454 --> 00:04:50.248
- Did you know that?
- No.


00:04:50.332 --> 00:04:53.210
He was born and raised here,


00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:56.046
and he swore he'd never leave.


00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:03.345
He said that Mississippi
was the place of miracles.


00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:07.390
You think he'll give us our miracle?


00:05:10.352 --> 00:05:11.520
[Maben] <i>Yeah, I do.</i>


00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:14.397
<i>I think he's...</i>


00:05:15.357 --> 00:05:16.817
[sniffles]


00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:18.735
<i>...out there, watching us...</i>


00:05:20.487 --> 00:05:22.739
<i>making sure that we're doing okay.</i>


00:05:27.828 --> 00:05:30.121
- I love you.
- Mm, I love you too, baby.


00:05:30.205 --> 00:05:32.082
- Good night.
- You gotta go to sleep.


00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:34.751
- Okay. Good night.
- Good night.


00:05:44.845 --> 00:05:48.223
[somber music playing]


00:06:41.902 --> 00:06:43.904
[traffic passing by]


00:07:07.427 --> 00:07:09.429
[siren whoops]


00:07:12.307 --> 00:07:13.350
[patrol car door closes]


00:07:16.478 --> 00:07:18.688
- What are you doing?
- Going back to my room.


00:07:20.815 --> 00:07:24.110
Excuse me. I just wanna have
a conversation with you, ma'am.


00:07:24.194 --> 00:07:25.737
Please don't disrespect me.


00:07:27.864 --> 00:07:28.865
Thank you.


00:07:29.616 --> 00:07:31.534
Now I'm guessing you know it's not legal


00:07:31.618 --> 00:07:33.536
to go in them trucks
and do them dirty things.


00:07:34.371 --> 00:07:35.747
I didn't go in no truck.


00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:37.749
Now I saw you coming down off them steps.


00:07:38.833 --> 00:07:40.043
Ned called us.


00:07:41.169 --> 00:07:43.922
All right? He's tired of y'all
trashing up his parking lot.


00:07:44.005 --> 00:07:46.257
See, this here is a family establishment.


00:07:46.341 --> 00:07:48.051
Well, I didn't do nothin', so...


00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:50.178
- Y'all never do.
- What are you doin'... Hey!


00:07:50.261 --> 00:07:52.097
I told you that I didn't do...
I didn't do anything!


00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:54.182
[Maben arguing in distance]


00:07:58.603 --> 00:08:00.188
- What are you doin'?!
- [Clint grunting]


00:08:00.271 --> 00:08:01.690
I got a kid in there, okay?


00:08:01.773 --> 00:08:03.108
- You can't do this.
- Shut your damn mouth!


00:08:03.191 --> 00:08:05.276
- I got a kid in there!
- Shut your damn mouth!


00:08:08.363 --> 00:08:11.241
[breathing heavily]


00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:13.493
- Hey... hey!
- [car door closes]


00:08:14.536 --> 00:08:17.664
Hey. I have my daughter in the room


00:08:17.747 --> 00:08:20.083
and you can't leave her in there, so...


00:08:20.166 --> 00:08:22.252
- And I'm telling you the truth.
- Y'all do drugs.


00:08:23.461 --> 00:08:26.006
See, I didn't leave her. You did.


00:08:27.757 --> 00:08:30.051
- [sobbing]
- Oh, stop crying.


00:08:30.135 --> 00:08:32.512
Now you're not going to jail.


00:08:32.595 --> 00:08:34.472
And if you were,
I'd have cuffed you already.


00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:36.725
You just sit back and relax.


00:08:37.642 --> 00:08:39.019
And if you're a good little girl,


00:08:39.769 --> 00:08:41.312
if you're quieter than
a little church mouse,


00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:44.941
you might even get back to your kid
quicker than you think.


00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:47.444
[distant train horn]


00:08:55.785 --> 00:08:58.079
Now I know you know
I'm about to come back there.


00:08:59.581 --> 00:09:01.207
A girl like you shouldn't mind.


00:09:02.667 --> 00:09:05.003
- [rustling]
- See?


00:09:07.088 --> 00:09:08.423
I ain't gonna hurt you.


00:09:09.716 --> 00:09:11.426
Maybe we could even be friends.


00:09:15.555 --> 00:09:17.307
How about a little mood lighting?


00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:19.517
- [switch clicks]
- That better?


00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:21.311
[car door opens]


00:09:28.026 --> 00:09:31.029
[tense music playing]


00:09:36.117 --> 00:09:37.702
Take off them dirty shoes.


00:09:43.374 --> 00:09:44.876
[shoes falling]


00:09:52.217 --> 00:09:53.218
Good girl.


00:09:54.552 --> 00:09:55.678
Now the rest.


00:10:10.568 --> 00:10:12.445
Now swing them legs over to me.


00:10:19.077 --> 00:10:20.203
There you go.


00:10:24.791 --> 00:10:26.835
If you wanna see that motel room again...


00:10:28.253 --> 00:10:29.796
you better goddamn behave.


00:10:36.678 --> 00:10:38.096
[belt buckle clinks]


00:10:41.808 --> 00:10:44.811
[tense music playing]


00:10:47.105 --> 00:10:48.690
[thumping]


00:11:29.772 --> 00:11:33.276
I wouldn't worry about that.
We ain't done just yet.


00:11:35.445 --> 00:11:36.529
- You hear me?!
- [gasps]


00:11:36.613 --> 00:11:37.989
Take it back off.


00:11:45.955 --> 00:11:47.457
I thought that was what you wanted.


00:11:48.583 --> 00:11:49.959
Yeah, it was.


00:11:58.593 --> 00:12:01.429
I did what you told me to do.


00:12:01.512 --> 00:12:04.224
And you said that you would
take me back to my kid.


00:12:04.307 --> 00:12:05.808
What do you think would happen


00:12:05.892 --> 00:12:08.478
if that kid's momma
got picked up for prostitution,


00:12:08.561 --> 00:12:11.397
kid left there alone
in that shitty motel room?


00:12:12.273 --> 00:12:15.485
There's no food
or nothing in there either. Huh?


00:12:16.986 --> 00:12:19.447
[phone line ringing]


00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:20.657
Hey, old boy.


00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:22.367
Got us some new entertainment.


00:12:23.993 --> 00:12:25.912
Well, why don't you come on out
and I'll show you?


00:12:25.995 --> 00:12:28.122
[Clint laughing]


00:12:28.206 --> 00:12:30.708
Same spot. Y'all can both come.


00:12:30.792 --> 00:12:32.669
[chuckles] Yeah.


00:12:35.171 --> 00:12:36.464
Gon' be a party!


00:12:37.966 --> 00:12:39.550
We're gonna have us some company.


00:12:41.803 --> 00:12:45.181
You want me to go out
on the hood and wait for 'em?


00:12:45.265 --> 00:12:46.724
Well, now that's the spirit!


00:12:48.059 --> 00:12:49.519
And why not?


00:12:49.602 --> 00:12:50.937
Be a nice hood ornament.


00:12:52.647 --> 00:12:54.107
Don't put nothin' on.


00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:57.443
[Clint whistling]


00:13:00.029 --> 00:13:01.197
Come on, then.


00:13:16.796 --> 00:13:19.007
[resumes whistling]


00:13:26.931 --> 00:13:28.224
Ain't got all night.


00:13:30.226 --> 00:13:33.521
- Attagirl.
- [winces] It's hot.


00:13:34.605 --> 00:13:35.982
Yeah?


00:13:36.065 --> 00:13:37.734
Can I get my shirt to sit on?


00:13:38.776 --> 00:13:39.777
Go on.


00:13:41.571 --> 00:13:42.739
Hurry up.


00:13:45.116 --> 00:13:47.118
- [whistling]
- [suspenseful music playing]


00:14:00.506 --> 00:14:02.550
[Clint laughing]


00:14:02.633 --> 00:14:03.634
Whoa, now.


00:14:04.344 --> 00:14:05.887
Are you fuckin' kidding me?


00:14:07.388 --> 00:14:09.724
Don't you know not
to play with guns, girl, huh?


00:14:09.807 --> 00:14:12.185
- That ain't a toy. Put it down!
- [grunts]


00:14:12.268 --> 00:14:13.353
[casings clinking]


00:14:14.729 --> 00:14:17.732
[dramatic music playing]


00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:30.912
[gasping]


00:14:55.561 --> 00:14:56.979
[passing car honking]


00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:17.917
[Analee screaming] Mommy!


00:15:19.919 --> 00:15:21.295
[crying]


00:15:21.379 --> 00:15:23.798
[screaming]


00:15:28.428 --> 00:15:31.639
[crying, screaming]


00:15:33.391 --> 00:15:35.184
I know, baby, hang on.


00:15:36.185 --> 00:15:38.229
- [sobbing]
- [Analee wailing]


00:15:44.902 --> 00:15:47.488
It's okay. Hey, baby.


00:15:47.572 --> 00:15:50.158
Hey, I'm here, baby.


00:15:50.241 --> 00:15:53.327
It's okay, shh...


00:15:53.411 --> 00:15:57.498
- [wailing continues]
- I know, I know, I'm so sorry.


00:15:57.582 --> 00:16:00.585
[dramatic music continues]


00:16:19.312 --> 00:16:21.647
[soft music playing]


00:16:25.318 --> 00:16:26.569
[distant honking]


00:17:19.789 --> 00:17:22.959
- [brakes squealing]
- [bus hisses]


00:17:40.726 --> 00:17:41.727
[bag rustling]


00:17:51.487 --> 00:17:52.488
Welcome home.


00:17:53.239 --> 00:17:54.740
- [grunts]
- [groans]


00:17:54.824 --> 00:17:57.326
[grunting continues]


00:17:57.410 --> 00:18:00.162
[blows and kicks landing]


00:18:01.289 --> 00:18:02.164
Hey...


00:18:05.543 --> 00:18:07.211
[Larry] They let you out early...


00:18:07.295 --> 00:18:10.673
- [Russell coughing]
- ...but you still owe, motherfucker.


00:18:10.756 --> 00:18:13.259
- You still owe.
- [man] Hey!


00:18:13.342 --> 00:18:15.386
Hey, stop it right there
or I'll call the law.


00:18:15.469 --> 00:18:17.179
- [Walt] Well, call 'em, asshole!
- I will call them.


00:18:17.263 --> 00:18:18.723
Just back off and go on!


00:18:20.099 --> 00:18:21.475
[Larry] Don't you worry.


00:18:22.226 --> 00:18:23.853
You ain't out of my reach, boy.


00:18:34.322 --> 00:18:35.531
You all right, man?


00:18:36.532 --> 00:18:37.658
Jesus.


00:18:54.133 --> 00:18:55.885
Home, sweet fucking home.


00:18:57.720 --> 00:18:59.722
[soft music playing]


00:19:29.001 --> 00:19:30.378
[water splashing]


00:19:37.051 --> 00:19:38.135
Hey, there, old man.


00:19:46.644 --> 00:19:47.937
[deep sigh]


00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:49.980
Heads up would have been nice.


00:19:50.064 --> 00:19:51.399
Told you I was getting out soon.


00:19:51.482 --> 00:19:52.983
Well, I could've come pick you up.


00:19:53.067 --> 00:19:54.318
Nah, I didn't want to bother you.


00:19:55.027 --> 00:19:56.112
Nah, it were no bother.


00:19:57.029 --> 00:19:58.989
[chokes up] Ahem.


00:19:59.073 --> 00:20:00.533
This here's Consuela.


00:20:02.201 --> 00:20:05.287
<i>- Es mi hijo.</i>
- <i>Sí.</i> Same eyes.


00:20:05.371 --> 00:20:07.331
- [chuckles]
<i>- Mucho gusto.</i>


00:20:09.125 --> 00:20:10.209
Nice to meet you.


00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:14.171
Speaking of eyes,
what happened to your face?


00:20:14.255 --> 00:20:17.007
Just a little going away present
from the boys on the inside,


00:20:17.091 --> 00:20:18.718
- I suppose.
- Hmm.


00:20:21.554 --> 00:20:23.431
I figure he could use
a little meat on his bones.


00:20:23.514 --> 00:20:24.807
This woman can cook.


00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:27.351
Come on, you look like you need
something to eat. Come here.


00:20:27.435 --> 00:20:29.019
Jeez, I just walked all the way over here.


00:20:29.103 --> 00:20:30.104
Oh, hell.


00:20:31.313 --> 00:20:32.690
Where'd she come from?


00:20:35.067 --> 00:20:38.112
I went to visit your uncle Clive
down in Bogalusa.


00:20:38.195 --> 00:20:40.740
I saw her working in the sugar cane field.


00:20:42.283 --> 00:20:45.244
Big brown eyes kept watching me
everywhere I went,


00:20:45.327 --> 00:20:46.620
and she kept laughing at me.


00:20:47.496 --> 00:20:49.957
Anyway, I figured I'd go and ask her
why she was laughing.


00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:54.128
I mean, you should've seen how he had them
workers livin', in them ratty shacks,


00:20:54.211 --> 00:20:57.339
and... she didn't have
nobody and neither did I, so...


00:20:58.299 --> 00:21:00.176
I asked her if she wanted
to come and stay with me,


00:21:00.259 --> 00:21:02.553
and she said yes
and she's been here ever since.


00:21:02.636 --> 00:21:04.472
- And the rest is history.
- Yep.


00:21:04.555 --> 00:21:06.557
You're speaking Spanish now.


00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:09.059
<i>Muy poco,</i> but she gets it.


00:21:10.519 --> 00:21:12.396
I'll bet she does, you sly dog.


00:21:12.480 --> 00:21:14.523
It ain't like that.
You get your mind out of the gutter.


00:21:15.399 --> 00:21:16.776
Where she sleep?


00:21:16.859 --> 00:21:19.403
Um, in your old room, in the barn.


00:21:19.487 --> 00:21:22.239
- You liar.
- Oh, gimme that.


00:21:22.323 --> 00:21:23.240
[Mitchell chuckles]


00:21:29.538 --> 00:21:30.539
[Mitchell sighs]


00:21:40.424 --> 00:21:43.260
It got awful quiet here
when your mama passed.


00:21:46.555 --> 00:21:49.475
Some nights I'd sit out here and...


00:21:51.352 --> 00:21:53.979
it sounded as if the world
had come to an end.


00:21:58.526 --> 00:22:00.569
I tried to quit feeling bad about it.


00:22:01.362 --> 00:22:03.197
I hope your mama understands.


00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:06.450
Oh, I can't figure she'd mind.


00:22:06.534 --> 00:22:09.245
You can't feel any worse
about her than I do.


00:22:10.454 --> 00:22:14.291
I know it hurt her,
me being where I was while she was dying.


00:22:17.378 --> 00:22:20.089
Well, she loved you.
And that's all that matters.


00:22:26.011 --> 00:22:29.682
I wrote you a bunch of letters
I didn't send.


00:22:29.765 --> 00:22:32.351
You know, I figured you didn't need
the extra weight.


00:22:33.936 --> 00:22:36.105
You didn't need more shit,
mine or anyone else's.


00:22:36.188 --> 00:22:37.857
Well, that's okay. I'm here now.


00:22:39.400 --> 00:22:40.818
Give me all the shit you got.


00:22:40.901 --> 00:22:41.902
[Mitchell chuckles]


00:22:45.990 --> 00:22:47.908
[object rattles]


00:22:47.992 --> 00:22:50.035
You still got that old thing, huh?


00:22:50.953 --> 00:22:52.454
You talkin' about the Bible?


00:22:54.415 --> 00:22:55.916
She and I sit out here,


00:22:56.000 --> 00:22:58.419
helps her with her English. She reads.


00:22:58.502 --> 00:23:01.088
Just like you and me used to read
when you was learnin', remember?


00:23:01.171 --> 00:23:03.757
- Yeah, I remember.
- You used to love those old stories.


00:23:03.841 --> 00:23:05.342
Daniel in the lion's den
was your favorite.


00:23:05.426 --> 00:23:08.178
I don't really believe
in none of that no more.


00:23:08.262 --> 00:23:09.930
What, that the lions didn't eat him?


00:23:10.014 --> 00:23:12.057
Nah. I don't believe in none of it.


00:23:16.020 --> 00:23:18.981
I used to go to these prison chapel
meetings sometimes.


00:23:19.064 --> 00:23:21.400
An old white-haired preacher,
a bunch of outlaws


00:23:21.483 --> 00:23:23.819
sittin' in all these folding chairs,


00:23:23.903 --> 00:23:26.113
yelling their hallelujahs.


00:23:28.032 --> 00:23:30.659
Preacher'd get up, give his sermon.


00:23:30.743 --> 00:23:32.202
And everybody get to take turns,


00:23:32.286 --> 00:23:34.663
getting up at the pulpit,
give their testimonies.


00:23:34.747 --> 00:23:36.040
"Yes, I stole."


00:23:36.123 --> 00:23:37.291
"Yes, I raped."


00:23:37.374 --> 00:23:40.377
"Yes, I beat the shit
out of my fellow man."


00:23:41.545 --> 00:23:44.715
"But now I found the love of God,
now I see the light."


00:23:44.798 --> 00:23:46.300
And so on, and so on,


00:23:46.383 --> 00:23:48.677
and all their clappings
and "amens," and shit,


00:23:48.761 --> 00:23:51.555
and I just didn't care for it,
so I stopped going.


00:23:51.639 --> 00:23:52.890
Hmm.


00:23:55.684 --> 00:23:57.019
Do you think it's fair?


00:23:57.102 --> 00:24:00.105
- What? Do I think what's fair?
- Tsk...


00:24:00.981 --> 00:24:03.776
Well, that man can get
into the magic Kingdom


00:24:03.859 --> 00:24:06.278
no matter what they done,


00:24:06.362 --> 00:24:08.530
as long as they say the magic words.


00:24:09.823 --> 00:24:11.867
Words have power if you mean them.


00:24:13.285 --> 00:24:15.746
And it doesn't matter
what you and me think is fair.


00:24:17.331 --> 00:24:18.832
This Good Book


00:24:18.916 --> 00:24:21.126
tells me that the door is always open.


00:24:22.503 --> 00:24:25.547
Let me ask you something.
How's what you did different?


00:24:25.631 --> 00:24:28.592
'Cause I made one big fucking mistake!


00:24:29.927 --> 00:24:31.428
And I didn't mean it. They meant it.


00:24:31.512 --> 00:24:34.264
Damn right. And you ain't them.


00:24:34.348 --> 00:24:36.684
You made a big fucking mistake


00:24:36.767 --> 00:24:38.602
and you did your time for it.


00:24:38.686 --> 00:24:40.396
Well, in whose eyes?


00:24:42.022 --> 00:24:44.775
Mine? Theirs?


00:24:46.026 --> 00:24:49.947
I have an accident, I get swooped away
and locked away behind these bars.


00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:53.492
Don't get to show my remorse,
get my sorrys to nobody that I hurt.


00:24:53.575 --> 00:24:56.453
Ain't you, ain't me,
ain't nobody out there


00:24:56.537 --> 00:24:59.123
just gonna snap their fingers


00:24:59.206 --> 00:25:01.875
and instill some sort
of forgiveness in me.


00:25:03.919 --> 00:25:06.463
Son, you're being awful
damn hard on yourself.


00:25:10.551 --> 00:25:12.594
I got to believe we can be forgiven.


00:25:14.054 --> 00:25:16.849
'Cause if we can't,
well, then we're all fucked.


00:25:21.395 --> 00:25:22.479
[Mitchell chuckles]


00:25:23.897 --> 00:25:26.483
It was them boys that did
that to your face, wasn't it?


00:25:26.567 --> 00:25:28.652
Waitin' at the bus stop,
soon as I pulled in.


00:25:28.736 --> 00:25:30.279
Yeah, fuckin' Larry.


00:25:31.572 --> 00:25:33.407
Got you set up at, uh,


00:25:35.284 --> 00:25:38.871
one of my places there
at, uh, Michigan Avenue.


00:25:38.954 --> 00:25:40.873
Here's your car keys,
got the keys to the place...


00:25:40.956 --> 00:25:42.958
It's that old place we put
the shutters on, you remember?


00:25:43.042 --> 00:25:44.710
Oh, I know. How could I forget?


00:25:44.793 --> 00:25:47.629
Yeah, but, uh, listen,
why don't you just stay out here,


00:25:47.713 --> 00:25:49.965
you give those fellas
some time to cool off?


00:25:50.049 --> 00:25:52.509
Oh, they ain't coolin' off any time soon.


00:25:52.593 --> 00:25:53.927
'Sides, they know where you live.


00:25:54.011 --> 00:25:57.139
They can pull up the driveway
just as easy as I can.


00:25:58.515 --> 00:26:00.225
I ain't bringin' that out here.


00:26:02.519 --> 00:26:04.688
Well, I've got something for you.
Hang on to these.


00:26:14.531 --> 00:26:16.325
Here. [sighs]


00:26:19.369 --> 00:26:23.624
I don't recall anything about
no hunting rifle in the New Testament.


00:26:23.707 --> 00:26:27.920
Well, you can only turn so many cheeks,
and I only got four, so...


00:26:28.003 --> 00:26:32.174
I'd be breaking about two dozen laws
just by having it.


00:26:32.257 --> 00:26:34.134
I'd feel a whole lot better
knowing you're safe.


00:26:34.218 --> 00:26:37.429
- Ain't gon' be that bad.
- Well, you don't know how it's gonna get.


00:26:41.600 --> 00:26:42.601
Okay.


00:26:45.562 --> 00:26:47.689
[soft music playing]


00:26:47.773 --> 00:26:49.608
[Russell] <i>Do you ever think
about that moment?</i>


00:26:52.111 --> 00:26:54.363
<i>That moment I got
a little too big, too old,</i>


00:26:54.446 --> 00:26:56.281
<i>too heavy for you to carry?</i>


00:26:56.365 --> 00:27:00.452
<i>You think to yourself,
"Goddamn! I can't carry my son no more."</i>


00:27:03.872 --> 00:27:06.166
<i>You don't have to carry me no more, Dad.</i>


00:27:06.250 --> 00:27:07.459
[bag thuds]


00:27:07.543 --> 00:27:08.752
<i>I'll be okay.</i>


00:27:24.935 --> 00:27:26.937
- [door bell jingles]
- [indistinct chatter]


00:27:46.331 --> 00:27:48.625
- [waitress indistinct]
- Thank you.


00:27:50.919 --> 00:27:52.171
Shot of Bug, please.


00:27:53.589 --> 00:27:54.798
[pool balls clatter]


00:27:58.010 --> 00:27:59.469
- [whooping]
- [bottles clinking]


00:28:05.225 --> 00:28:06.643
[laughter]


00:28:13.817 --> 00:28:16.653
[muffled screaming]


00:28:22.534 --> 00:28:24.411
[breathing heavily]


00:28:26.580 --> 00:28:28.582
- [insects chirping]
- [soft music continues]


00:29:44.074 --> 00:29:45.200
[siren whoops]


00:29:50.872 --> 00:29:53.083
Get out of the truck! Show me your hands!


00:30:00.382 --> 00:30:01.383
Slowly.


00:30:09.933 --> 00:30:13.520
Get that goddamn thing
out of my face, Boyd!


00:30:13.603 --> 00:30:15.022
[laughing]


00:30:15.105 --> 00:30:16.356
Well, I'll be damned!


00:30:16.982 --> 00:30:18.483
- When'd you get home?
- Noon.


00:30:18.567 --> 00:30:20.527
- Noon today?
- Noon today.


00:30:21.320 --> 00:30:22.654
Give me some love, man. Don't stand there.


00:30:22.738 --> 00:30:24.031
- All right.
- [both grunting]


00:30:24.114 --> 00:30:26.533
[both chuckling]


00:30:26.616 --> 00:30:29.661
- Ow! Stop it.
- [laughter]


00:30:29.745 --> 00:30:31.580
We grown now.
You can't be lifting me up like that.


00:30:31.663 --> 00:30:33.999
- Oh, I got you.
- [Boyd laughs]


00:30:35.042 --> 00:30:36.209
Well, talk to me. How was it?


00:30:37.044 --> 00:30:40.130
About what you can imagine,
'cept way fucking worse.


00:30:42.507 --> 00:30:45.135
How's Lacey? She still turning backflips?


00:30:45.218 --> 00:30:48.263
God, no. She couldn't put her right leg
in that old cheerleader outfit


00:30:48.347 --> 00:30:50.640
- if she wanted to.
- [both laugh]


00:30:50.724 --> 00:30:52.559
You gotta love her,
though, man. You got to.


00:30:54.770 --> 00:30:56.021
So what's goin' on here?


00:30:57.314 --> 00:30:58.857
[Boyd] Ain't no point
in keeping it a secret.


00:30:58.940 --> 00:31:00.650
Be on the news tomorrow.


00:31:00.734 --> 00:31:04.029
One of our own shot with his own pistol,
which we can't seem to find.


00:31:04.905 --> 00:31:06.907
- Shit.
- [distant train horn]


00:31:06.990 --> 00:31:08.283
Anyone I know?


00:31:08.367 --> 00:31:12.037
Nah, this guy came down from Tupelo
or somewhere a year or two back.


00:31:13.205 --> 00:31:14.873
Been on thin ice ever since he got here.


00:31:14.956 --> 00:31:17.834
So I wouldn't be surprised
if something catch back up to his ass.


00:31:18.710 --> 00:31:20.962
Just hate for Lacey
to find out about this one.


00:31:21.046 --> 00:31:23.465
She stays worried enough
about me, you know?


00:31:23.548 --> 00:31:25.008
Oh, I bet.


00:31:25.092 --> 00:31:27.594
Well, they're gonna ask me
if I checked you out, so...


00:31:28.387 --> 00:31:30.472
I gotta check you out,
see what's in the truck.


00:31:30.555 --> 00:31:32.808
Okay, yeah. Open it up.


00:31:43.151 --> 00:31:45.529
Russ, you ain't been out 24 hours.


00:31:45.612 --> 00:31:47.280
Shit, man! You know you ain't supposed
to have no gun.


00:31:48.740 --> 00:31:51.368
Just got out of the damn cage, Boyd.


00:31:51.451 --> 00:31:52.953
You don't know what that feels like.


00:31:53.036 --> 00:31:54.955
- You wanna go back to the cage?
- No.


00:31:55.038 --> 00:31:58.125
Didn't think so, so if I was you,
get in the truck and call it a night.


00:32:01.253 --> 00:32:02.462
Yes, officer.


00:32:07.175 --> 00:32:10.178
[suspenseful music playing]


00:32:19.396 --> 00:32:20.689
[Brenda] <i>This is it.</i>


00:32:22.107 --> 00:32:24.651
You have the whole place to yourselves.


00:32:24.734 --> 00:32:27.154
The doors lock at 8 p.m.


00:32:27.237 --> 00:32:29.865
If you go out,
you need a password to get in.


00:32:29.948 --> 00:32:32.659
Oh, hey, you wait.
You let me help you get up there.


00:32:32.742 --> 00:32:34.202
Well, let me help put your bags away.


00:32:34.286 --> 00:32:36.830
No. We're good.


00:32:38.457 --> 00:32:39.458
Is, uh...


00:32:39.541 --> 00:32:42.836
Is there anything I can do for-for work?
I mean, I'll do just about anything.


00:32:42.919 --> 00:32:44.880
There's a bar up the road


00:32:44.963 --> 00:32:47.382
where you can help with the dishes
and work in the kitchen.


00:32:47.466 --> 00:32:50.927
Now, it ain't much,
but he pays out at the end of the day.


00:32:52.929 --> 00:32:54.347
Can I work today?


00:32:55.474 --> 00:32:56.975
You look like you need a break.


00:32:57.767 --> 00:32:58.768
I don't.


00:33:00.103 --> 00:33:01.813
You sure nobody's following you?


00:33:02.439 --> 00:33:03.648
We get that.


00:33:06.735 --> 00:33:09.070
Didn't you tell her
that she could have a hot dog?


00:33:09.154 --> 00:33:10.071
Hmm?


00:33:10.864 --> 00:33:13.200
- You want a hot dog?
- Come on, baby.


00:33:28.381 --> 00:33:31.384
[somber music playing]


00:33:38.558 --> 00:33:40.894
[birds chirping]


00:33:58.203 --> 00:34:01.706
Sometimes I have a hard time
remembering how old he'd be.


00:34:02.666 --> 00:34:06.169
I ride by here just to remind myself.
You ever do that?


00:34:06.253 --> 00:34:07.754
I could say at anytime...


00:34:08.755 --> 00:34:10.423
exactly how old he'd be.


00:34:11.925 --> 00:34:13.969
Twenty-five years, three months.


00:34:14.594 --> 00:34:16.096
Yeah, I wish I could do that.


00:34:18.348 --> 00:34:19.349
It's all right.


00:34:20.058 --> 00:34:22.602
You got a busy life, you got a family.


00:34:24.020 --> 00:34:25.522
Ain't nobody blamin' you.


00:34:28.108 --> 00:34:31.736
Besides... I remember enough
for the both of us.


00:34:33.196 --> 00:34:34.197
[sniffles]


00:34:39.744 --> 00:34:41.079
Why do you always do that?


00:34:43.039 --> 00:34:44.040
His toll.


00:34:45.417 --> 00:34:46.626
To bring him home.


00:34:48.670 --> 00:34:50.338
There's always a price to pay.


00:35:01.850 --> 00:35:02.851
I like that.


00:35:07.814 --> 00:35:10.775
[laughing]


00:35:10.859 --> 00:35:13.987
Man, it's no wonder these boys
are stacked like brick houses,


00:35:14.070 --> 00:35:16.448
- you feedin' them like that.
- Well, they're hearty eaters.


00:35:16.531 --> 00:35:17.532
Boys...


00:35:18.992 --> 00:35:21.119
Well, I thank you much, Lacey.


00:35:21.202 --> 00:35:23.955
- That was damn good.
- We're just glad you're home.


00:35:24.039 --> 00:35:26.541
I'm just glad these boys took after you.


00:35:26.625 --> 00:35:30.045
- [laughs] Your mouth to God's ears.
- [Boyd] Hey, now.


00:35:33.006 --> 00:35:35.091
Oh, I see you're up to mischief.


00:35:35.175 --> 00:35:36.926
[glasses clink]


00:35:37.010 --> 00:35:38.970
- 'Bout that time?
- [dishes rattling]


00:35:39.054 --> 00:35:42.307
Don't act like you don't know. [sighs]


00:35:59.949 --> 00:36:02.243
Why the hell you didn't call me
knowing you was getting out?


00:36:02.327 --> 00:36:06.081
Hmm? You know I would've drove
down there and got you.


00:36:08.041 --> 00:36:09.959
You know it don't work like that.


00:36:10.043 --> 00:36:12.253
Tsk, see, uh...


00:36:12.337 --> 00:36:13.797
that's where you're wrong.


00:36:13.880 --> 00:36:15.507
- [glass rattles]
- I got special privileges.


00:36:16.466 --> 00:36:18.051
Flash 'em the old badge.


00:36:18.134 --> 00:36:20.762
[both laughing]


00:36:20.845 --> 00:36:22.931
- Special privileges.
- Well, I'll just show 'em mine.


00:36:23.014 --> 00:36:24.391
That didn't work anyways.


00:36:24.474 --> 00:36:25.934
- And it's bigger.
- [Boyd laughing]


00:36:26.017 --> 00:36:28.728
Always has been, always will be.


00:36:28.812 --> 00:36:31.398
[chuckling]


00:36:31.481 --> 00:36:32.857
All fools.


00:36:35.485 --> 00:36:37.821
Tsk. Larry had it figured.


00:36:39.906 --> 00:36:41.700
That's what happened to your face?


00:36:41.783 --> 00:36:42.867
Sure is.


00:36:44.035 --> 00:36:45.954
How serious do you think the brothers are?


00:36:46.037 --> 00:36:48.832
Oh, I don't know
how serious they are together.


00:36:48.915 --> 00:36:51.084
I know Larry's pretty serious
all on his own.


00:36:52.961 --> 00:36:54.170
You want me to go say something?


00:36:54.254 --> 00:36:55.755
- 'Cause you know I will.
- No. Shit, no.


00:36:55.839 --> 00:36:58.341
I've dealt with way worse
since the last time I saw you.


00:36:58.425 --> 00:37:00.927
Besides, Larry's just a puppy dog,
comparatively speaking.


00:37:01.010 --> 00:37:04.723
Yeah, an aggravating,
chew-up-your-shit puppy dog, though.


00:37:04.806 --> 00:37:06.558
There's a big difference.


00:37:06.641 --> 00:37:08.017
[grunts] Well, you know...


00:37:12.230 --> 00:37:14.149
How you doin'? You doin' okay?


00:37:14.774 --> 00:37:15.859
Doing good.


00:37:18.278 --> 00:37:20.155
Russ, come on.


00:37:20.238 --> 00:37:21.698
How you really doin'?


00:37:24.200 --> 00:37:25.952
Thought I'd feel a little different.


00:37:26.035 --> 00:37:27.996
Feels good all at the same time, but...


00:37:28.747 --> 00:37:29.831
I don't know.


00:37:31.332 --> 00:37:32.542
You seen her yet?


00:37:33.460 --> 00:37:34.878
No, not yet.


00:37:35.879 --> 00:37:40.216
But it's a small town,
I'm bound to run into her sooner or later.


00:37:40.300 --> 00:37:43.052
[chuckles] Man...


00:37:43.136 --> 00:37:46.139
We burned up a lot of miles
and a lot of time out on those roads.


00:37:47.557 --> 00:37:48.558
I missed that.


00:37:50.977 --> 00:37:52.729
Turns out, I missed you too, bro.


00:37:53.480 --> 00:37:56.733
Oh, don't get all gushy on me.


00:37:58.818 --> 00:38:00.320
I missed you too, bud.


00:38:00.403 --> 00:38:02.822
I knew it. I knew it.


00:38:06.326 --> 00:38:08.286
[insects chirping]


00:38:13.333 --> 00:38:17.045
- [suspenseful music playing]
- [tapping on flask]


00:38:42.862 --> 00:38:43.863
[cuts engine]


00:39:23.987 --> 00:39:25.154
[curtain rings rattle]


00:39:46.759 --> 00:39:47.844
[light thud]


00:40:02.859 --> 00:40:05.862
[tense music playing]


00:40:14.829 --> 00:40:16.831
[birds chirping]


00:40:26.341 --> 00:40:27.592
[door creaks]


00:40:37.852 --> 00:40:39.395
[Russell] <i>How long have you been here?</i>


00:40:40.688 --> 00:40:41.731
[Sarah] <i>All morning.</i>


00:40:43.107 --> 00:40:45.109
<i>Hadn't gotten up the courage to knock.</i>


00:40:47.153 --> 00:40:48.988
You look the same.


00:40:49.072 --> 00:40:51.616
- [laughs] Please.
- You do.


00:40:53.451 --> 00:40:54.369
Well...


00:40:55.203 --> 00:40:56.996
you look like you could use a hot meal.


00:40:58.373 --> 00:41:02.710
You know, people keep saying that to me,
but nobody's offered to buy me any dinner.


00:41:02.794 --> 00:41:04.212
[Sarah chuckles softly]


00:41:07.006 --> 00:41:08.049
You all right?


00:41:11.928 --> 00:41:13.304
Yeah, I'm okay.


00:41:15.890 --> 00:41:16.724
You?


00:41:17.976 --> 00:41:20.311
[sighs] Oh, yes.


00:41:21.354 --> 00:41:22.647
I'm all right.


00:41:28.611 --> 00:41:30.905
I bet your daddy's happy that you're home.


00:41:33.908 --> 00:41:35.660
I was sorry about your mama.


00:41:36.703 --> 00:41:37.704
Yeah...


00:41:39.288 --> 00:41:41.165
[sniffles] Yeah, boy.


00:41:42.333 --> 00:41:45.086
Sure would've been nice
for her to see me make it.


00:41:48.423 --> 00:41:50.216
I bet she's smiling.


00:41:56.973 --> 00:41:58.182
Remodeling?


00:42:00.518 --> 00:42:02.437
Oh, hurricane last night.


00:42:02.520 --> 00:42:04.188
[laughing] I bet.


00:42:04.272 --> 00:42:05.815
That hurricane got a name?


00:42:05.898 --> 00:42:07.275
Oh, they usually do.


00:42:07.358 --> 00:42:08.568
[chuckles]


00:42:18.327 --> 00:42:19.912
You still mad at me?


00:42:21.998 --> 00:42:24.000
I told you then like I'll tell you now.


00:42:25.543 --> 00:42:27.170
Ain't nothing to be mad about.


00:42:31.215 --> 00:42:33.426
Seems like you told me the same thing.


00:42:35.053 --> 00:42:36.095
I knows it.


00:42:38.056 --> 00:42:39.390
I just wondered.


00:42:42.518 --> 00:42:45.688
I'm the one that told you
to stop coming to see me.


00:42:48.024 --> 00:42:49.942
But I'm the one who agreed.


00:42:59.410 --> 00:43:00.578
How many kids?


00:43:02.455 --> 00:43:05.541
I got twin boys and a little girl.


00:43:05.625 --> 00:43:06.834
How old?


00:43:09.212 --> 00:43:12.673
My boys are four and the girl is two.


00:43:23.434 --> 00:43:26.729
Man, all I want to do
is hold your hand right now.


00:43:28.231 --> 00:43:29.690
Just for one minute.


00:43:38.074 --> 00:43:40.076
[melancholy music playing]


00:43:42.495 --> 00:43:43.579
[Sarah sniffles]


00:43:49.043 --> 00:43:50.086
[kisses]


00:43:54.173 --> 00:43:55.842
[Sarah sobbing]


00:44:22.285 --> 00:44:24.662
There's a whole lot between us now.


00:44:28.499 --> 00:44:30.084
[sighs] A whole lot...


00:44:36.883 --> 00:44:38.843
I can't keep it anymore.


00:44:40.761 --> 00:44:42.180
But it's yours.


00:44:43.931 --> 00:44:45.016
It was.


00:44:47.101 --> 00:44:49.478
[sniffles] I gotta go.


00:44:49.562 --> 00:44:52.565
[melancholic music continues]


00:45:06.329 --> 00:45:07.538
[dishes clatter]


00:45:25.264 --> 00:45:28.267
[soft music playing]


00:45:37.652 --> 00:45:38.861
[Maben] Hello.


00:45:39.904 --> 00:45:42.657
- Mommy!
- [laughs]


00:45:42.740 --> 00:45:45.534
Hi, baby. Thank you for watching her.


00:45:47.203 --> 00:45:49.288
- What are you doing?
- Coloring.


00:45:49.372 --> 00:45:51.332
- Red? Too scary. Too scary.
- [chuckles]


00:45:51.415 --> 00:45:52.833
- Purple!
- Yeah!


00:45:52.917 --> 00:45:56.379
Purple, a really nice light...


00:45:56.462 --> 00:45:58.923
- shade of purple.
- Yeah.


00:45:59.006 --> 00:46:00.549
[Analee] <i>Tell me about Daddy.</i>


00:46:04.095 --> 00:46:05.346
Well...


00:46:06.764 --> 00:46:08.391
<i>You have his eyes.</i>


00:46:08.474 --> 00:46:10.017
<i>- I do?
- Mm-hmm.</i>


00:46:11.143 --> 00:46:12.144
<i>And...</i>


00:46:13.062 --> 00:46:17.233
<i>he would've been able
to make you laugh so hard</i>


00:46:17.316 --> 00:46:19.694
<i>that I think you would've broken ribs.</i>


00:46:20.403 --> 00:46:21.612
[Maben chuckles]


00:46:23.906 --> 00:46:25.491
<i>And he was just...</i>


00:46:27.535 --> 00:46:28.869
so real.


00:46:29.912 --> 00:46:31.622
And so kind.


00:46:33.666 --> 00:46:35.584
<i>And he was my first everything.</i>


00:46:38.963 --> 00:46:40.548
And together we made you.


00:46:42.925 --> 00:46:44.135
And you're...


00:46:45.428 --> 00:46:48.431
the most important thing
in the whole world, do you know that?


00:46:51.600 --> 00:46:52.601
Hmm?


00:47:00.109 --> 00:47:02.653
[soft music playing]


00:47:06.615 --> 00:47:09.160
- Analee... Analee, where's our stuff?
- Yeah?


00:47:09.243 --> 00:47:10.453
In there?


00:47:14.040 --> 00:47:15.291
Who told you to empty the bag?


00:47:15.374 --> 00:47:17.668
I-I-I didn't do it. The lady did.


00:47:18.878 --> 00:47:20.463
[gasps]


00:47:21.672 --> 00:47:24.550
- Get on your shoes.
- [stammering] What for?


00:47:24.633 --> 00:47:27.887
Do what I say and put your shoes on
and get your stuff.


00:47:27.970 --> 00:47:29.430
But I don't wanna go!


00:47:29.513 --> 00:47:32.308
Baby, shh! I know you wanna stay here,


00:47:32.391 --> 00:47:34.977
- but we gotta go.
- W-what's happening?


00:47:35.061 --> 00:47:37.730
Just listen to me.
Do what I say and put your shoes on.


00:47:37.813 --> 00:47:39.273
And get the rest of your stuff over there.


00:47:39.357 --> 00:47:41.359
- You said we could stop walking...
- I know what I said.


00:47:41.442 --> 00:47:44.195
- ...once we got to Mississippi...
- Hey! Baby!


00:47:44.278 --> 00:47:46.947
Look at me. I love you.
I'm gonna take care of you,


00:47:47.031 --> 00:47:49.742
but you gotta do what I'm telling you
to do right now. Do you get it?


00:47:52.703 --> 00:47:54.580
- Mommy, where are we going?
- [shushes]


00:47:55.748 --> 00:47:57.249
I want my crayons.


00:47:59.460 --> 00:48:00.711
- Mommy!
- Shh!


00:48:06.884 --> 00:48:08.302
[whispering] Okay, this way.


00:48:10.304 --> 00:48:13.724
Okay. Now you have to be so quiet.


00:48:14.892 --> 00:48:16.018
No talking.


00:48:17.061 --> 00:48:19.438
We're playing the silent game
and you wanna win, right?


00:48:19.522 --> 00:48:20.439
Yeah.


00:48:25.528 --> 00:48:27.571
- I want my crayons.
- Shh.


00:48:29.407 --> 00:48:32.326
- You're gonna lose if you say anything.
- [quietly] Okay.


00:48:38.874 --> 00:48:40.376
[Brenda on phone] I don't know...


00:48:40.459 --> 00:48:41.627
[Analee sneezes loudly]


00:48:42.795 --> 00:48:45.131
I found it unpacking their clothes.


00:48:47.508 --> 00:48:50.010
I get the feeling
they're in some kind of trouble.


00:48:52.638 --> 00:48:55.099
[breathing heavily] Okay.


00:48:55.182 --> 00:48:57.393
Okay, listen to me, baby girl.


00:48:59.019 --> 00:49:01.564
Mommy messed up, okay?


00:49:01.647 --> 00:49:04.650
I messed up really bad. Big mistake.


00:49:05.443 --> 00:49:07.153
But you wanna stay with Mommy, right?


00:49:08.529 --> 00:49:10.781
'Cause I really want to stay with you


00:49:10.865 --> 00:49:12.992
and, if we're gonna stay together,


00:49:13.075 --> 00:49:15.661
we have to go right now.


00:49:15.744 --> 00:49:18.497
And you have to do exactly
what I'm about to tell you to do, okay?


00:49:19.457 --> 00:49:20.583
- Yeah?
- Yeah.


00:49:23.294 --> 00:49:25.296
[suspenseful music playing]


00:49:32.595 --> 00:49:33.888
[Analee whispering] Can we go yet?


00:49:36.223 --> 00:49:37.224
[Maben] Okay.


00:49:38.517 --> 00:49:40.769
Okay. Go. Go!


00:50:25.314 --> 00:50:26.941
[phone ringing]


00:50:31.278 --> 00:50:32.321
[Brenda] Hello?


00:50:34.448 --> 00:50:36.700
Wait. Where's Analee?


00:50:38.244 --> 00:50:39.537
She's not in the room?


00:50:42.164 --> 00:50:43.415
Is the mother back?


00:50:51.715 --> 00:50:53.676
[distant clattering]


00:50:53.759 --> 00:50:55.261
[door opens]


00:50:57.304 --> 00:50:58.305
Hello?


00:51:02.142 --> 00:51:04.061
Analee, is that you, honey?


00:51:06.021 --> 00:51:07.481
Is anyone there?


00:51:09.108 --> 00:51:12.111
[dramatic music playing]


00:51:16.031 --> 00:51:17.866
[grunting, panting]


00:51:38.470 --> 00:51:39.471
[lighter clicks]


00:52:05.664 --> 00:52:06.874
- [Maben] Don't move.
- [gun clicks]


00:52:08.959 --> 00:52:10.127
Get in the truck.


00:52:12.671 --> 00:52:15.507
Will you get in the truck? All right?


00:52:15.591 --> 00:52:17.343
- I'm goin'.
- Hurry up.


00:52:38.614 --> 00:52:42.034
Okay, just turn on the car.
Turn on the car and drive!


00:52:42.993 --> 00:52:45.120
- [engine turns over]
- Where?


00:52:45.204 --> 00:52:48.666
Just-just go. Get a...
Get away from the lights.


00:52:49.416 --> 00:52:50.626
North, go North.


00:52:55.547 --> 00:52:56.840
- [Analee] Mama?
- [Maben] Yeah, baby.


00:52:56.924 --> 00:52:59.134
I gotta pee really badly.


00:53:01.220 --> 00:53:03.597
Okay, how bad do you have to pee?


00:53:03.681 --> 00:53:06.475
- Really badly. Can we stop, please?
- We'll find her a place.


00:53:07.976 --> 00:53:09.520
I got a place for you to pee.


00:53:11.563 --> 00:53:13.565
And you can lower that pistol as well.


00:53:14.483 --> 00:53:17.569
Lot of potholes out here,
don't need you accidentally shooting me.


00:53:17.653 --> 00:53:20.155
Didn't come this far
to have it read on my tombstone


00:53:20.239 --> 00:53:22.241
"Accidentally shot by some woman."


00:53:26.078 --> 00:53:28.163
If I shoot you, it's not an accident.


00:53:31.583 --> 00:53:33.627
Tsk. Understood.


00:53:34.420 --> 00:53:37.005
[vehicle pulls over]


00:53:37.256 --> 00:53:38.799
[sets parking brake]


00:53:40.259 --> 00:53:43.429
You hurry up. Okay? Go pee fast...


00:53:43.512 --> 00:53:45.264
Hey! No. No!


00:53:46.432 --> 00:53:47.850
Fucking give that back to me.


00:53:47.933 --> 00:53:49.768
Oh, I think I'll hold on to that.


00:53:51.437 --> 00:53:52.980
[gun clicking]


00:53:58.819 --> 00:54:00.362
This ain't your gun.


00:54:03.699 --> 00:54:05.909
Can you just give me back that gun?


00:54:05.993 --> 00:54:08.120
You can empty it out, I don't care, just...


00:54:09.371 --> 00:54:11.331
- Just give it back to me.
- I will...


00:54:12.124 --> 00:54:13.959
when you tell me who it belongs to.


00:54:14.042 --> 00:54:16.253
- [Maben sighs]
- [rain pattering]


00:54:22.217 --> 00:54:23.886
I tried to fix all this...


00:54:26.513 --> 00:54:27.931
before it even started.


00:54:29.266 --> 00:54:30.934
You know, I went down...


00:54:33.145 --> 00:54:35.939
to this place in New Orleans
when I found out I was pregnant.


00:54:36.023 --> 00:54:37.733
I thought it was the right thing to do.


00:54:39.401 --> 00:54:40.736
Maybe it was.


00:54:46.158 --> 00:54:47.326
But as I...


00:54:49.077 --> 00:54:52.080
As I was sittin' there,
in that room, waiting,


00:54:52.164 --> 00:54:54.249
and I don't know,
I just started thinking that, you know,


00:54:54.333 --> 00:54:56.502
maybe everything was going to be okay.


00:54:59.087 --> 00:55:01.423
[voice breaking]
I've tried so fucking hard...


00:55:03.467 --> 00:55:06.470
You know, I actually didn't even know
a person could, uh...


00:55:08.972 --> 00:55:10.349
could try that hard.


00:55:11.016 --> 00:55:13.227
[sniffs] But you know, uh...


00:55:13.310 --> 00:55:15.938
[sniffs] nowhere worked out.


00:55:16.021 --> 00:55:18.398
Not Shreveport, not...


00:55:18.482 --> 00:55:21.777
not Beaumont, not Lake Charles, and...


00:55:26.031 --> 00:55:27.616
I can't feed her.


00:55:30.202 --> 00:55:32.454
[weeping] I can't put clothes on her.


00:55:34.164 --> 00:55:37.918
I can't give her a fucking place to sleep
and now this.


00:55:38.001 --> 00:55:40.546
So yeah... [sniffles] Uh...


00:55:41.713 --> 00:55:44.341
If you could just leave us here...


00:55:45.884 --> 00:55:46.885
Please...


00:55:46.969 --> 00:55:48.804
And what about your family?


00:55:50.722 --> 00:55:52.933
What about her daddy?
What about your mama?


00:55:55.811 --> 00:55:57.813
[smacks lips] Not everybody has somebody.


00:55:59.106 --> 00:56:00.524
[rain pattering]


00:56:07.114 --> 00:56:08.824
So where to now?


00:56:11.410 --> 00:56:12.452
[stammers]


00:56:12.536 --> 00:56:14.329
I'll make you a promise.


00:56:14.413 --> 00:56:19.042
I'll drive you anywhere, within reason.


00:56:20.002 --> 00:56:21.962
But we're gonna take a rest tonight.


00:56:23.213 --> 00:56:24.047
Okay?


00:56:33.307 --> 00:56:34.933
[Maben] <i>I knew it wasn't gonna end.</i>


00:56:36.852 --> 00:56:40.522
<i>All I could see was her face.</i>


00:56:40.606 --> 00:56:42.357
Thinking that I'd left her,


00:56:42.441 --> 00:56:45.277
thinking that nobody in the whole world
cared about her.


00:56:50.240 --> 00:56:51.992
So I stole his gun and I shot him.


00:56:52.075 --> 00:56:54.244
I shot him until he wasn't movin' no more.


00:57:03.670 --> 00:57:05.672
But you don't look like a killer to me.


00:57:08.091 --> 00:57:10.427
I've seen plenty,
I know what they look like.


00:57:13.430 --> 00:57:15.182
[fire crackling]


00:57:15.265 --> 00:57:16.642
[cigarette rustling in box]


00:57:23.815 --> 00:57:26.693
Why are you holdin' on
to that gun, anyway?


00:57:28.445 --> 00:57:30.489
You know that damn thing will bury you.


00:57:33.075 --> 00:57:36.536
If there's one thing in the world
that could bury you...


00:57:38.205 --> 00:57:39.998
would you wanna know where it was?


00:57:43.752 --> 00:57:45.087
What's your name?


00:57:55.722 --> 00:57:58.141
- [insects chirping]
- [soft music playing]


00:58:02.354 --> 00:58:03.397
[grunting softly]


00:58:06.942 --> 00:58:07.943
[Maben] Got her?


00:58:09.736 --> 00:58:12.239
You guys just sleep in here.
I'll take the back.


00:58:19.788 --> 00:58:20.789
Maben.


00:58:25.877 --> 00:58:27.087
My name's Maben.


00:58:33.427 --> 00:58:34.428
I'm Russell.


00:58:59.369 --> 00:59:00.454
Maben...


00:59:05.208 --> 00:59:06.918
You gotta be kiddin' me.


00:59:13.717 --> 00:59:14.801
Cody?


00:59:17.721 --> 00:59:19.431
Cody, boy.


00:59:21.725 --> 00:59:23.101
Big papa's home.


00:59:24.895 --> 00:59:25.771
Big...


00:59:26.730 --> 00:59:29.608
Hey. Hey, I... Look, I know that it's...


00:59:29.691 --> 00:59:32.861
- You're not supposed to be here.
- [stammering] I-I know. I know, I know.


00:59:32.944 --> 00:59:36.323
- Go on, Larry. Go on. Come on.
- Look, look, is-is he here?


00:59:37.365 --> 00:59:40.077
- Is Cody here?
- 'Course he's here.


00:59:40.744 --> 00:59:43.580
- Could I-could I see him for a minute?
- Oh, Larry.


00:59:43.663 --> 00:59:45.707
- It's the middle of the night.
- Baby, baby, please, please.


00:59:45.791 --> 00:59:48.585
- No, it's the middle of the night.
- I just wanna see him for a minute.


00:59:50.837 --> 00:59:51.755
[sighs]


00:59:52.589 --> 00:59:54.174
I see you've been drinking.


00:59:57.219 --> 00:59:59.471
Yeah. Yeah, I've been drinking.


01:00:07.646 --> 01:00:10.107
I just got one question, okay?


01:00:10.190 --> 01:00:12.984
Is-is-is he still playing Little League?


01:00:14.945 --> 01:00:18.532
- [sighs]
- Is he still playing? Is he-is he...


01:00:18.615 --> 01:00:21.409
Is he swinging the bat
like his Daddy showed him?


01:00:21.493 --> 01:00:24.871
[sobbing] He's too big
for Little League, Larry!


01:00:24.955 --> 01:00:26.498
Goddammit! [sobs]


01:00:26.581 --> 01:00:29.042
You'd know that if you saw him.


01:00:29.126 --> 01:00:31.336
Well, fuck! You won't let me see him.


01:00:31.419 --> 01:00:34.047
That ain't fuckin' fair! What are you
talking about, "if I saw him"?


01:00:34.131 --> 01:00:35.966
I've been tryin' to see him,
that's why I'm here!


01:00:36.049 --> 01:00:39.010
Get sober and you can see your son.


01:00:39.094 --> 01:00:41.596
- That's what I said.
- [yelling] I'm fuckin' trying!


01:00:41.680 --> 01:00:43.390
- Not hard enough!
- Cody, boy!


01:00:43.473 --> 01:00:46.852
You fuckin' be quiet!
We got a restraining order.


01:00:46.935 --> 01:00:48.937
I don't wanna have to call
somebody, please.


01:00:49.020 --> 01:00:51.189
Who the fuck you gonna call? Huh?


01:00:51.273 --> 01:00:54.526
You fuckin' call 'em! I remember
that restraining order. Fuck you!


01:00:54.609 --> 01:00:56.611
- Call! You call!
- I will fuckin' call somebody out here.


01:00:56.695 --> 01:00:59.614
I will call somebody out here.
You get out! Get out!


01:01:01.324 --> 01:01:02.742
- You hear that, boy?
- [door opens]


01:01:02.826 --> 01:01:05.453
Your Daddy's out here, trying to see you!


01:01:06.413 --> 01:01:07.414
[door closes]


01:01:09.124 --> 01:01:11.960
Don't ever fuckin' say I didn't try, boy!


01:01:14.129 --> 01:01:16.840
[sniffles] Don't ever say
I didn't fuckin...


01:01:16.923 --> 01:01:19.926
[somber music playing]


01:01:29.060 --> 01:01:32.230
- [distant howling]
- [sniffs]


01:01:32.314 --> 01:01:35.942
[loud howling]


01:01:39.738 --> 01:01:42.741
[howling continues]


01:01:46.369 --> 01:01:49.122
- [birds chirping]
- Baby girl.


01:01:49.206 --> 01:01:50.624
[kisses]


01:01:52.209 --> 01:01:54.294
[both speaking indistinct]


01:01:55.295 --> 01:01:56.379
Time to wake up.


01:01:57.464 --> 01:01:58.757
Okay.


01:02:01.218 --> 01:02:02.761
Did you sleep okay?


01:02:02.844 --> 01:02:04.387
- Yeah.
- Yeah?


01:02:08.600 --> 01:02:10.518
I have a present for you.


01:02:10.602 --> 01:02:12.604
- You do?
- Yeah, I forgot about it


01:02:12.687 --> 01:02:16.107
until I was lookin' at you
while you were asleep.


01:02:20.695 --> 01:02:22.280
Crayons?


01:02:23.365 --> 01:02:26.493
- In all of your favorite colors.
- Thank you, mama.


01:02:26.576 --> 01:02:28.245
- Thank you, mama.
- [chuckles]


01:02:36.002 --> 01:02:38.004
- [grunts]
- All right, who wants to get out of here


01:02:38.088 --> 01:02:40.173
and go get a bite to eat for breakfast?


01:02:41.132 --> 01:02:42.592
I got us a plan.


01:02:44.219 --> 01:02:45.512
What's the plan?


01:02:45.595 --> 01:02:47.514
I know a place you can go.


01:02:49.432 --> 01:02:50.642
Somewhere safe.


01:02:53.103 --> 01:02:55.814
If I'm gonna trust you,
you're gonna have to trust me.


01:02:57.440 --> 01:02:58.441
Okay?


01:03:00.277 --> 01:03:02.112
We're gonna get a little bite to eat, huh?


01:03:03.196 --> 01:03:05.782
- Yeah.
- Oh, we'll fill that belly.


01:03:05.865 --> 01:03:07.742
- [truck door opens]
- Sleep all right?


01:03:07.826 --> 01:03:08.827
[truck door closes]


01:03:11.454 --> 01:03:14.124
- [Boyd] <i>G'morning, Mr. Gaines.</i>
- [Mitchell] <i>Boyd!</i>


01:03:14.207 --> 01:03:15.583
[Boyd] <i>You happen to see Russell
this morning?</i>


01:03:15.667 --> 01:03:17.335
Uh, not yet.


01:03:17.419 --> 01:03:18.753
Any idea where he is?


01:03:18.837 --> 01:03:20.922
No, I was looking for 'im.
You went by the house?


01:03:21.006 --> 01:03:23.633
I did, I did, saw the windows.


01:03:24.384 --> 01:03:25.510
Is that what this is about?


01:03:27.429 --> 01:03:30.640
After we found our man,
Russell came drivin' up.


01:03:31.433 --> 01:03:34.686
Just him, nobody else all night,
way out there, so...


01:03:34.769 --> 01:03:36.104
I gotta ask him about it, that's all.


01:03:36.187 --> 01:03:38.231
Maybe he mighta seen
something that we're not?


01:03:39.024 --> 01:03:40.734
- That's it?
- That's it, I swear.


01:03:41.609 --> 01:03:44.237
- I'm sorry to hear about your man.
- Thank you.


01:03:45.363 --> 01:03:48.116
Yeah. Well, I just need his eyes.
Just have him call me, please?


01:03:48.199 --> 01:03:49.409
I will. Oh, and Boyd.


01:03:49.492 --> 01:03:51.828
Um, keep an eye on them boys, will you?


01:03:51.911 --> 01:03:53.204
Especially Larry.


01:03:53.288 --> 01:03:55.665
I can guarantee it was him
that busted out them windows.


01:03:56.333 --> 01:03:58.084
They already put a knot
on the side of his head


01:03:58.168 --> 01:03:59.669
when they met him at the bus station.


01:04:01.963 --> 01:04:02.964
I'll pay attention.


01:04:04.049 --> 01:04:05.091
Thanks, Boyd.


01:04:07.344 --> 01:04:09.179
[insects chirping]


01:04:14.642 --> 01:04:16.061
[Russell] You girls sit tight here.


01:04:20.482 --> 01:04:21.775
Got some company.


01:04:27.322 --> 01:04:29.324
Oh, it's good to see
you're still breathing.


01:04:29.407 --> 01:04:31.701
You gotta remember,
there's people who give a shit about you.


01:04:33.995 --> 01:04:35.330
What the hell is going on?


01:04:35.997 --> 01:04:38.458
I mean, the place was all busted up,
I assume you didn't do it.


01:04:38.541 --> 01:04:40.418
I ain't worried
about none of that right now.


01:04:40.502 --> 01:04:41.336
[Mitchell] Mm.


01:04:42.253 --> 01:04:44.714
I'm gonna ask you a question,
all I need is a yes or no.


01:04:45.590 --> 01:04:48.134
I need that old place
in the barn for them.


01:04:49.219 --> 01:04:50.678
I'll explain everything later.


01:04:50.762 --> 01:04:53.473
Boyd was snooping around,
I mean, something you ain't tellin' me.


01:04:53.556 --> 01:04:54.974
Yes or no, that's all I need.


01:04:55.058 --> 01:04:56.726
Oh, yeah, there's something
you ain't telling me.


01:04:56.810 --> 01:04:59.187
All right, well, I got your back.


01:04:59.270 --> 01:05:01.314
But you got... you know,
don't keep me in the dark here.


01:05:04.692 --> 01:05:06.361
I want you to pretend


01:05:06.444 --> 01:05:08.947
it's that first time you saw Consuela...


01:05:10.156 --> 01:05:12.784
and you did what you did
because you thought it was right.


01:05:14.786 --> 01:05:17.705
- [exhales sharply]
- They look hungry. I make food.


01:05:18.706 --> 01:05:20.667
Very kind of you, Consuela. Thank you.


01:05:21.584 --> 01:05:23.503
One more thing.
Don't tell anyone they're here.


01:05:23.586 --> 01:05:25.338
Well, I'm not a complete idiot.


01:05:28.591 --> 01:05:30.218
[barn doors rumbling]


01:05:36.683 --> 01:05:38.143
- [Maben] It's pretty big.
- Well...


01:05:38.977 --> 01:05:40.103
Here it is.


01:05:42.355 --> 01:05:43.356
Go on in.


01:05:49.112 --> 01:05:52.991
Bet you probably expected something
to go moo when you came in then.


01:05:53.074 --> 01:05:54.117
[Maben chuckles]


01:06:05.545 --> 01:06:07.630
Hopefully this is comfortable for y'all.


01:06:09.883 --> 01:06:11.509
Bathroom is right over there.


01:06:12.594 --> 01:06:14.304
Don't judge a book by its cover.


01:06:15.472 --> 01:06:16.473
It's nice.


01:06:18.308 --> 01:06:20.393
I'll get you maybe some water.


01:06:20.477 --> 01:06:23.646
Hey! I know your mama probably said...


01:06:24.939 --> 01:06:26.858
there's no jumping on the bed.


01:06:27.692 --> 01:06:29.861
Well, if there's one bed
in this whole world


01:06:29.944 --> 01:06:32.113
that you can jump off, it's...


01:06:32.780 --> 01:06:33.823
it's this one.


01:06:34.949 --> 01:06:37.911
You jump on that with everything
your life's got to give.


01:06:37.994 --> 01:06:40.914
- [Analee] Okay.
- I don't hear you jumping.


01:06:42.040 --> 01:06:44.459
[Analee giggles] Thank you!


01:06:46.252 --> 01:06:49.255
- [pensive music playing]
- [bird cawing]


01:06:51.049 --> 01:06:53.927
[Mitchell] All right, slow and steady.


01:06:55.678 --> 01:06:56.596
Okay!


01:06:56.679 --> 01:06:58.640
[Analee] Look, mama! I caught another one.


01:06:58.723 --> 01:07:01.476
Look at that! Call it beginner's luck!


01:07:01.559 --> 01:07:04.479
- [Analee giggling]
- Could've used this kid as bait!


01:07:04.562 --> 01:07:05.563
[Analee laughs]


01:07:07.649 --> 01:07:09.275
You gonna catch another one out here?


01:07:09.359 --> 01:07:10.527
We're working on it.


01:07:11.194 --> 01:07:13.571
- [Analee] Trying to.
- What's even out there, huh?


01:07:13.655 --> 01:07:15.156
[Analee] Catfish.


01:07:18.076 --> 01:07:19.285
[Russell] <i>Hey, Mama.</i>


01:07:20.912 --> 01:07:21.955
<i>I'm home.</i>


01:07:25.917 --> 01:07:28.628
<i>I'm doing somethin' right now
that I think is right.</i>


01:07:30.046 --> 01:07:31.464
<i>I'm helpin' someone.</i>


01:07:34.175 --> 01:07:36.135
<i>I know you're watching over me.</i>


01:07:38.137 --> 01:07:39.973
<i>I'll try and do right by you.</i>


01:07:42.809 --> 01:07:45.436
Anyways, I just wanted to say I love you.


01:07:48.856 --> 01:07:50.984
I love you more than anything.


01:07:53.361 --> 01:07:54.946
[cheers and applause]


01:07:55.572 --> 01:07:58.992
There he is! There's my boy!
You swing, motherfucker!


01:08:00.034 --> 01:08:01.411
Swing it!


01:08:01.494 --> 01:08:03.871
Swing at those fuckin' fastballs, Cody!


01:08:03.955 --> 01:08:05.957
How many times I done told you?


01:08:06.040 --> 01:08:08.876
How many times I done told you?


01:08:08.960 --> 01:08:11.588
- Huh? You swing...
- Hey! What are you doing here?


01:08:11.671 --> 01:08:14.549
- Hey! How you doin', Dana?
- You can't be here.


01:08:15.758 --> 01:08:18.136
- I can be... I can watch my fuckin' boy...
- No, you can't!


01:08:18.219 --> 01:08:20.805
- You can't be here and you know it!
- Shut the fuck up! Get the fuck out...


01:08:20.888 --> 01:08:22.181
I ain't gonna fuckin' hurt him...


01:08:22.265 --> 01:08:24.267
- I ain't gonna fuckin' hurt nobody!
- Don't do this here!


01:08:24.350 --> 01:08:26.561
- [crying] Please, Larry!
- Hey, get over here, boy.


01:08:27.604 --> 01:08:30.773
- Hey! You get over here, boy.
- Hey!


01:08:30.857 --> 01:08:32.942
- You don't need to talk to him, Cody!
- Shut the fuck up!


01:08:33.026 --> 01:08:35.820
You shut up!
Don't talk to him, Cody! [crying]


01:08:35.903 --> 01:08:38.489
What you doin' out there, boy?
You swing at those fastballs.


01:08:38.573 --> 01:08:40.199
- You don't take 'em.
- I'm tryin' to play.


01:08:40.283 --> 01:08:43.494
Look, I'll come down here.
I'll show you how to play.


01:08:43.578 --> 01:08:46.247
- I'll show you how to play.
- I don't need your help.


01:08:47.874 --> 01:08:49.667
That's not what it looks like, boy.


01:08:50.918 --> 01:08:52.670
Hey... hey!


01:08:53.588 --> 01:08:56.007
- Hey!
- [Cody] I ain't talkin' to you!


01:08:56.090 --> 01:08:57.467
You ain't talkin' to me?


01:08:58.760 --> 01:09:01.888
You ain't talkin' to me?!
You ain't talkin' to me?!


01:09:01.971 --> 01:09:04.641
You ain't talkin' to me?! Huh?


01:09:05.642 --> 01:09:08.061
I'm your goddamn father, you motherfucker!


01:09:10.647 --> 01:09:14.067
What kind of boy don't talk
to his own goddamn father?!


01:09:14.150 --> 01:09:17.987
What kind of fuckin' boy don't...
what, motherfucker?


01:09:18.071 --> 01:09:20.323
- What? Sit the fuck down!
- [people clamoring]


01:09:20.406 --> 01:09:24.077
- [siren wailing]
- You ugly-ass, sorry-ass motherfuckers.


01:09:26.371 --> 01:09:27.497
[siren whoops]


01:09:27.580 --> 01:09:30.249
- Oh, you gon' done called them again?
- [Dana] Yeah, I did.


01:09:30.333 --> 01:09:32.001
You stay right the fuck there.


01:09:33.670 --> 01:09:34.754
- What, you think I was gon' hit you
- [Jay] Larry!


01:09:34.837 --> 01:09:35.838
- With this?
- [gasps]


01:09:35.922 --> 01:09:37.882
- You think I was gon' hit you with this?
- I fuckin' know it.


01:09:37.965 --> 01:09:40.426
Fuck you, Jay. Fuck you, Jay.


01:09:40.510 --> 01:09:42.595
- You don't need to come down here...
- Come on, think about that...


01:09:42.679 --> 01:09:44.055
Come on, come on...


01:09:44.138 --> 01:09:46.015
- [grunting]
- Dammit, Larry!


01:09:49.644 --> 01:09:51.479
I'm your goddamn father!


01:09:52.271 --> 01:09:53.940
[groans] You're my boy!


01:09:54.691 --> 01:09:56.818
Don't fuckin' listen to her.


01:09:56.901 --> 01:09:59.362
- She'll ruin your fuckin' life, son!
- Come on, enough!


01:09:59.445 --> 01:10:01.322
She'll ruin your fuckin' life!


01:10:03.241 --> 01:10:05.410
[insects chirping]


01:10:08.996 --> 01:10:10.415
[Maben] What are we doing here?


01:10:17.088 --> 01:10:19.799
Try not to look at me
when I tell you this.


01:10:25.972 --> 01:10:27.598
I was in an argument one night


01:10:28.766 --> 01:10:30.268
'bout my relationship.


01:10:33.104 --> 01:10:36.315
<i>Done some wrongs,
beat myself up pretty bad over it.</i>


01:10:39.068 --> 01:10:42.947
<i>Driving around on back roads,
started drinkin'...</i>


01:10:43.030 --> 01:10:44.157
[tires screeching]


01:10:44.240 --> 01:10:46.909
<i>Drinkin' a lot, feelin' pretty good...</i>


01:10:47.952 --> 01:10:49.495
<i>Just drivin' the night away.</i>


01:10:51.998 --> 01:10:55.293
<i>All of a sudden, I get turned around.</i>


01:10:56.836 --> 01:10:58.838
<i>Got lost on the way and...</i>


01:10:58.921 --> 01:11:00.506
[revs]


01:11:00.590 --> 01:11:02.550
...started going pretty fast.


01:11:07.472 --> 01:11:09.599
All of a sudden, I come up over this hill.


01:11:11.851 --> 01:11:14.395
There was a truck
right in the middle of the road,


01:11:14.479 --> 01:11:15.688
lights off.


01:11:19.150 --> 01:11:22.153
[melancholic music playing]


01:11:41.047 --> 01:11:42.048
Hi.


01:11:44.091 --> 01:11:46.844
[breathes deeply, shudders]


01:11:46.928 --> 01:11:48.095
I'm cold.


01:11:49.555 --> 01:11:50.807
Let me get you my jacket.


01:11:58.147 --> 01:12:01.150
- [vehicle approaching]
- Hey! Hey!


01:12:02.902 --> 01:12:04.403
- Jason!
- [brakes screeching]


01:12:05.530 --> 01:12:07.740
I couldn't slam on the brakes fast enough.


01:12:09.534 --> 01:12:10.952
<i>Next thing I know,</i>


01:12:11.035 --> 01:12:13.704
<i>- my whole left side's all crushed up...</i>
- Jason! Jason!


01:12:13.788 --> 01:12:16.916
<i>- ...someone's screaming...</i>
- Jason!


01:12:18.251 --> 01:12:19.585
[screaming] Help! Please help me!


01:12:19.669 --> 01:12:21.045
[Russell] <i>And that's
when I left that truck...</i>


01:12:21.128 --> 01:12:22.880
[Maben screaming indistinctly]


01:12:22.964 --> 01:12:25.967
<i>- Poor soul that was inside.</i>
- [Maben screaming]


01:12:32.306 --> 01:12:35.560
Had a feeling you might know
what I'm talking about here.


01:12:38.229 --> 01:12:39.230
[gasps]


01:12:43.025 --> 01:12:44.318
Thought you were in jail.


01:12:45.486 --> 01:12:46.529
Got out...


01:12:47.572 --> 01:12:48.990
a few days ago.


01:12:59.584 --> 01:13:01.294
[catches breath]


01:13:02.378 --> 01:13:04.088
I hated you.


01:13:07.550 --> 01:13:11.554
Oh, my God, I hated you.
I hated you so fuckin' much.


01:13:13.556 --> 01:13:14.724
I used to pray


01:13:16.100 --> 01:13:17.101
every night...


01:13:18.185 --> 01:13:20.396
that somebody was beatin' you,


01:13:21.272 --> 01:13:22.815
holdin' you down...


01:13:25.067 --> 01:13:27.653
I used to pray for hours.


01:13:29.488 --> 01:13:31.198
And one day, I just got tired of it.


01:13:32.241 --> 01:13:34.035
I got tired of it, I got tired of...


01:13:36.829 --> 01:13:38.789
Got too tired to hate you...


01:13:39.540 --> 01:13:40.833
anymore.


01:13:45.087 --> 01:13:47.256
But then, I was a long way from here...


01:13:48.799 --> 01:13:50.134
running on fumes.


01:13:51.260 --> 01:13:54.889
Trying to save my own life...


01:13:58.059 --> 01:13:59.352
save Analee's...


01:14:01.312 --> 01:14:02.355
And you...


01:14:03.814 --> 01:14:04.815
you...


01:14:06.859 --> 01:14:08.277
didn't matter.


01:14:10.112 --> 01:14:11.322
At all.


01:14:13.032 --> 01:14:14.784
How old is Analee, Maben?


01:14:16.911 --> 01:14:18.788
How old do you think she is?


01:14:20.790 --> 01:14:23.626
Maben, I've been praying
that wasn't the case.


01:14:23.709 --> 01:14:27.171
I swear to God, I've been praying
that wasn't the case.


01:14:31.634 --> 01:14:34.720
Larry and Walt know? They know about her?


01:14:37.556 --> 01:14:39.058
Don't see how they would.


01:14:41.644 --> 01:14:43.479
[sighs]


01:14:43.562 --> 01:14:47.024
- Goddamn, I'm sorry.
- No, don't...


01:14:48.317 --> 01:14:52.238
I didn't get to tell you then,
so I'm sayin' it now that I'm...


01:14:52.321 --> 01:14:54.824
- I'm sorry.
- No!


01:14:54.907 --> 01:14:57.118
- I'm sayin' I'm sorry...
- No, you don't get to apologize


01:14:57.201 --> 01:14:58.744
'cause it don't change nothing.


01:14:58.828 --> 01:15:01.330
It might make you feel better,
but it don't change nothing.


01:15:01.414 --> 01:15:05.126
- It don't make me feel any better...
- Do not fuckin' say it again!


01:15:13.134 --> 01:15:14.510
We gotta throw this.


01:15:15.511 --> 01:15:18.305
You think you can pay for that
with a splash?


01:15:18.389 --> 01:15:20.558
I already paid for it.


01:15:22.309 --> 01:15:26.689
The only person I owe is that boy
and I'll be paying for that soon enough.


01:15:29.191 --> 01:15:31.318
Shit, I believe everything you say.


01:15:32.570 --> 01:15:35.072
And I'm glad you shot that asshole.


01:15:35.156 --> 01:15:36.991
I don't know who he was, but...


01:15:38.200 --> 01:15:40.453
I can see him in my mind. Shit, I...


01:15:40.536 --> 01:15:44.331
Been many times I wished I had a gun
to shoot whoever had a hold on me.


01:15:45.458 --> 01:15:48.419
Been many times God
heard your prayers and He...


01:15:49.170 --> 01:15:52.715
He damn sure answered to you,
be sure He's up there.


01:15:53.591 --> 01:15:55.801
He heard me that time. [sniffs]


01:15:56.719 --> 01:15:57.845
Not no other time.


01:15:59.221 --> 01:16:00.639
Let me ask you...


01:16:03.726 --> 01:16:05.352
Why weren't you in the truck?


01:16:15.529 --> 01:16:16.572
[sighs]


01:16:16.655 --> 01:16:19.658
[dramatic music playing]


01:16:27.416 --> 01:16:28.834
I guess so...


01:16:32.004 --> 01:16:34.006
so we can be standing here...


01:16:35.925 --> 01:16:37.009
right now.


01:16:42.473 --> 01:16:44.308
Well, I'll tell you one thing...


01:16:46.477 --> 01:16:49.480
They're gonna have to kill me
before I go back to prison.


01:16:49.563 --> 01:16:53.567
I know you already killed once
when the world had you by the throat...


01:16:55.402 --> 01:16:58.114
I'll do the same damn thing
before I go back.


01:16:59.865 --> 01:17:00.991
You hear me?


01:17:03.577 --> 01:17:05.579
Wait, um... wait.


01:17:09.834 --> 01:17:10.835
I'll do it.


01:17:15.881 --> 01:17:17.091
[Russell] Wipe it down.


01:17:26.350 --> 01:17:27.351
[sniffs]


01:17:40.698 --> 01:17:41.699
[exhales sharply]


01:18:02.469 --> 01:18:04.013
What are you doing here, bud?


01:18:04.930 --> 01:18:07.474
You know me. Waitin'.


01:18:08.392 --> 01:18:11.353
- Where you've been?
- Out at Mitchell's.


01:18:12.521 --> 01:18:14.273
Tell you I came out there
lookin' for you?


01:18:14.940 --> 01:18:17.943
- Well... found me.
- I have now.


01:18:18.027 --> 01:18:20.487
You know I've been huntin'
for you for a couple of days, right?


01:18:21.655 --> 01:18:23.490
Why don't you just tell me what you want?


01:18:24.742 --> 01:18:26.202
We got a dead cop, Russ.


01:18:26.285 --> 01:18:29.830
Between you and me, you're the only
one person be seen anywhere near him.


01:18:29.914 --> 01:18:32.791
Now, that don't mean nothing
other than we need to talk to you,


01:18:32.875 --> 01:18:35.252
but then when I come lookin' for you,
it takes me two days to find you.


01:18:35.336 --> 01:18:37.838
- So what?
- So where you been at?


01:18:37.922 --> 01:18:40.507
Comin' over here early in the morning,
late at night.


01:18:40.591 --> 01:18:42.259
Mitchell don't know.


01:18:42.343 --> 01:18:44.970
- You need to stop going out there.
- Then tell me what's going on,


01:18:45.054 --> 01:18:48.390
because your name is not the only name
that's been comin' across my desk.


01:18:48.474 --> 01:18:49.558
[paper rustling]


01:18:50.517 --> 01:18:51.560
What's that?


01:18:53.103 --> 01:18:54.772
You don't remember Maben?


01:18:54.855 --> 01:18:55.940
Why should I?


01:18:56.899 --> 01:18:59.109
Because it's the name of that gal


01:18:59.193 --> 01:19:01.028
that was with Jason
the night that he died.


01:19:01.111 --> 01:19:04.323
Figured a name like that
tied to a night like that, it might stick.


01:19:04.406 --> 01:19:06.867
I tried to forget all that.
Why are you showing me this?


01:19:10.371 --> 01:19:14.416
A woman named Maben came into
the shelter downtown with a little girl.


01:19:14.500 --> 01:19:16.877
The lady working there said
she found a pistol on her


01:19:16.961 --> 01:19:18.337
before she took off running.


01:19:18.420 --> 01:19:19.838
Now I know the last name is made up,


01:19:19.922 --> 01:19:23.008
but it's really hard
to make up a name like Maben.


01:19:24.635 --> 01:19:25.844
Tell me where you've been at.


01:19:25.928 --> 01:19:28.264
Look, you probably just missed me.


01:19:28.347 --> 01:19:29.807
Been out at Mitchell's.


01:19:30.683 --> 01:19:33.769
Larry's come by here, busted out
all my goddamn windows and doors,


01:19:33.852 --> 01:19:36.522
I ain't just gonna sit around here
waitin' for his ass to show up.


01:19:40.442 --> 01:19:43.696
Okay. You don't mind
if I ask Mitchell, do you?


01:19:43.779 --> 01:19:46.198
I just wanna clear your name,
so the department lays off me.


01:19:46.282 --> 01:19:48.617
Of course, go ahead. Just call 'im first.


01:19:48.701 --> 01:19:50.536
Don't just go showing up out there.


01:19:51.453 --> 01:19:53.580
Feel like enough burden as it is.


01:19:53.664 --> 01:19:55.874
All right, I hear you. I hear you.


01:19:55.958 --> 01:19:57.418
You know I hate asking you
these things, right?


01:19:57.501 --> 01:19:59.503
Yeah, whatever you say, bud.


01:20:00.963 --> 01:20:01.964
Love you.


01:20:03.799 --> 01:20:05.551
I'll pay you back for that bail.


01:20:06.135 --> 01:20:08.178
That's what you said last time.


01:20:08.262 --> 01:20:10.222
- Hey, come here.
- What? What?!


01:20:12.141 --> 01:20:13.434
Dude, what happened, man?


01:20:14.101 --> 01:20:15.185
It don't matter.


01:20:15.978 --> 01:20:18.814
- No, it... it does.
- What's the matter, motherfucker?


01:20:20.691 --> 01:20:22.401
I'm worried about you.


01:20:24.236 --> 01:20:27.448
Look, it's j... it's just us, man.


01:20:27.531 --> 01:20:29.450
We're all that's left, do you hear me?


01:20:31.410 --> 01:20:32.995
It don't... It ain't gon' bring him back.


01:20:33.620 --> 01:20:36.457
You gotta let him go, Larry.
It ain't gonna bring him back.


01:20:36.540 --> 01:20:38.500
You fuckin' one of them now.
You're one of them now.


01:20:39.668 --> 01:20:40.794
Don't say that shit, man.


01:20:40.878 --> 01:20:42.254
- Fuck you, man.
- Come on, man.


01:20:42.338 --> 01:20:44.340
- [kicks truck]
- Don't say that shit, dude.


01:20:44.423 --> 01:20:46.925
- Get the fuck out of here!
- Hey, you gotta calm down!


01:20:47.009 --> 01:20:48.719
You never had my back, motherfucker!


01:20:48.802 --> 01:20:50.304
Get the fuck out of here!


01:20:51.305 --> 01:20:52.765
Come on, man!


01:20:52.848 --> 01:20:55.726
- Pussy-ass motherfucker.
- Get back over here, man.


01:20:55.809 --> 01:20:58.937
Talk to me! I'm your brother!


01:20:59.021 --> 01:21:00.439
Fuckin' all there is


01:21:00.522 --> 01:21:03.984
- is out here, talkin' to myself.
- [truck departs]


01:21:04.068 --> 01:21:06.153
Just out here, talkin' to myself.


01:21:13.452 --> 01:21:15.829
[pensive music playing]


01:21:20.751 --> 01:21:22.378
Cody on first...


01:21:23.837 --> 01:21:26.840
Jason on second, Walt's on third.


01:21:27.424 --> 01:21:29.510
What's he do... he's callin' it!


01:21:30.177 --> 01:21:31.887
He's callin' it, y'all.


01:21:33.138 --> 01:21:34.473
Swings...


01:21:34.556 --> 01:21:37.184
- Fly fuckin' ball!
- [bat clatters]


01:21:37.267 --> 01:21:38.894
It's out of here!


01:21:39.603 --> 01:21:43.440
He's callin' it,
playing to the fuckin' crowd.


01:21:43.524 --> 01:21:46.318
[breathing heavily]


01:21:46.402 --> 01:21:47.444
He's making his way.


01:21:50.948 --> 01:21:52.950
[continues indistinct]


01:22:01.667 --> 01:22:03.085
He's making...


01:22:03.168 --> 01:22:04.795
[grunts]


01:22:09.508 --> 01:22:10.759
[sobbing]


01:22:17.349 --> 01:22:21.353
[music continues]


01:22:21.437 --> 01:22:24.857
[indistinct chatter]


01:22:32.906 --> 01:22:34.616
[indistinct chatter]


01:22:34.700 --> 01:22:36.410
- [laughing]
- [insects chirping]


01:22:38.996 --> 01:22:40.998
[Analee speaking indistinct]


01:23:07.649 --> 01:23:09.651
[Russell and Mitchell speaking indistinct]


01:23:12.821 --> 01:23:13.739
[laughing]


01:23:13.822 --> 01:23:17.534
[muted dialogue throughout]


01:23:57.282 --> 01:23:58.700
[knocking]


01:24:10.879 --> 01:24:13.382
[laughter]


01:24:14.508 --> 01:24:16.343
[tense music playing]


01:24:38.991 --> 01:24:39.992
[floor creaks]


01:24:49.084 --> 01:24:51.920
[footsteps coming up the stairs]


01:24:57.134 --> 01:24:59.094
- Hey! <i>¿Qué pasó?</i>
- Oh, shit, lady!


01:24:59.177 --> 01:25:00.721
- I was just looking for Mitchell.
<i>- Párele.</i>


01:25:00.804 --> 01:25:02.264
<i>- Usted no puede estar acá.</i>
- Okay. Relax.


01:25:02.347 --> 01:25:03.724
- Relax!
<i>- Váyase. Fuera de acá ya.</i>


01:25:03.807 --> 01:25:05.642
Settle down, okay?
Settle down, I'm leaving.


01:25:05.726 --> 01:25:08.812
<i>- Voy a llamar a la policía.</i>
- I am the damn police.


01:25:09.605 --> 01:25:10.814
[Mitchell] How you doin', Boyd?


01:25:10.897 --> 01:25:12.399
I mean, I wasn't plannin' on sellin',


01:25:12.482 --> 01:25:14.443
but, uh, feel free to have a look around.


01:25:15.235 --> 01:25:17.821
Knocked on the front door first.
Didn't hear anything.


01:25:17.904 --> 01:25:19.531
Thought I heard you out back,
so I went looking for you.


01:25:19.615 --> 01:25:21.908
Well, you were on the ball, Deputy.
Everything all right?


01:25:23.744 --> 01:25:26.705
I just need to know if Russell stayed here
with you the night before last.


01:25:26.788 --> 01:25:28.457
- Yeah, he did.
- All night?


01:25:29.249 --> 01:25:31.251
Well, I didn't set up all night
watching him snore or nothing,


01:25:31.335 --> 01:25:33.211
but, uh, as far as I know, he was here.


01:25:33.295 --> 01:25:35.213
Okay, good.
Anyone else can attest to that?


01:25:35.297 --> 01:25:37.007
Well, um, you musta seen 'im.


01:25:37.966 --> 01:25:38.967
Yes, I can.


01:25:40.218 --> 01:25:42.137
You speak English. Okay.


01:25:42.220 --> 01:25:44.222
Yeah, she'll do that... sometimes.


01:25:45.974 --> 01:25:48.101
All right. Thank you.


01:25:50.187 --> 01:25:51.438
Have a nice day, Deputy.


01:25:52.272 --> 01:25:53.690
[engine turns over]


01:26:02.616 --> 01:26:05.452
[car approaching]


01:26:06.912 --> 01:26:09.956
- [car door opens, closes]
- [whispering] Shit.


01:26:18.799 --> 01:26:20.759
You're lyin' to me
about where you've been.


01:26:20.842 --> 01:26:22.052
Your whole family is!


01:26:22.135 --> 01:26:23.762
What I can't understand is why.


01:26:25.305 --> 01:26:28.392
It don't matter what I say.
You got some big idea.


01:26:28.475 --> 01:26:30.727
Call it a big idea,
call it whatever you want.


01:26:31.728 --> 01:26:34.106
I'm here so you can talk to me, man. Me!


01:26:34.189 --> 01:26:37.150
Without talking to nobody else,
but you're not making it easy on me.


01:26:37.234 --> 01:26:38.652
Now when I get to that office,


01:26:38.735 --> 01:26:40.278
I'm gonna tell about
not being able to find you


01:26:40.362 --> 01:26:42.781
and about this woman named Maben,
who has a pistol on her,


01:26:42.864 --> 01:26:44.074
because you're leaving me no damn choice.


01:26:44.157 --> 01:26:46.076
Just because you didn't see me
lay down in bed


01:26:46.159 --> 01:26:47.452
don't mean I didn't sleep in it.


01:26:47.536 --> 01:26:49.830
Russell, there's ways
of getting to whatever it is


01:26:49.913 --> 01:26:52.249
you seem to be dancing around, man.
Talk to me!


01:26:52.332 --> 01:26:53.875
Then put the cuffs on me.


01:26:54.793 --> 01:26:56.002
Or get the hell out of here.


01:26:58.755 --> 01:27:00.590
Not until you answer me like I want.


01:27:02.968 --> 01:27:03.969
All right.


01:27:06.680 --> 01:27:09.266
You don't wanna leave? I will.


01:27:09.349 --> 01:27:10.767
[chair drags across floor]


01:27:12.936 --> 01:27:15.522
Wanna arrest me? Arrest me.


01:27:20.235 --> 01:27:22.070
Get the hell out of my damn house.


01:27:26.074 --> 01:27:29.077
[soft music playing]


01:27:33.206 --> 01:27:35.876
- Where's Mitchell?
- Yeah, you and me got to talk.


01:27:35.959 --> 01:27:38.920
- Boyd was back here snooping around...
- He see Maben or Analee?


01:27:39.004 --> 01:27:41.631
- [Consuela] Very close.
- What did you call her?


01:27:44.009 --> 01:27:45.093
You heard me.


01:27:51.892 --> 01:27:53.351
[Russell] <i>You're gonna have to go.</i>


01:27:54.394 --> 01:27:57.189
We're not talking about forever here,
Maben. We're talking about


01:27:57.272 --> 01:27:58.774
- a couple of weeks, okay?
- Yeah.


01:28:01.401 --> 01:28:02.986
Yeah. [sniffs]


01:28:04.321 --> 01:28:05.655
Just a... [sniffs]


01:28:05.739 --> 01:28:07.199
Just a couple of weeks.


01:28:07.282 --> 01:28:09.367
Hey, I don't see any other way around it.


01:28:11.870 --> 01:28:13.497
Been livin' that way for a while.


01:28:28.303 --> 01:28:29.805
We'll just sit out here.


01:28:31.681 --> 01:28:33.183
Let the sun go down.


01:28:34.976 --> 01:28:36.394
I bought you a bus ticket.


01:28:37.187 --> 01:28:39.523
[casings tinkle]


01:28:39.606 --> 01:28:41.149
There's one heading out late tonight.


01:28:42.484 --> 01:28:45.654
It'll take you to Memphis,
you just get off wherever you feel.


01:28:46.363 --> 01:28:48.865
I got you money too,
it's just all over at the house.


01:28:48.949 --> 01:28:51.785
No. I don't need your money.


01:28:51.868 --> 01:28:53.078
I know you don't.


01:28:55.705 --> 01:28:56.915
I don't need you to give me nothin'.


01:28:56.998 --> 01:28:58.625
I know I don't have to.


01:29:00.544 --> 01:29:02.379
Seems like you and I...


01:29:04.798 --> 01:29:07.884
we're tied together
by some sort of invisible rope,


01:29:07.968 --> 01:29:09.886
and it's always been there.


01:29:09.970 --> 01:29:11.805
It ain't lettin' us go.


01:29:16.101 --> 01:29:18.812
That girl's gonna be
damn fine sittin' here.


01:29:19.479 --> 01:29:21.523
You gotta get out of here,
you gotta be safe.


01:29:21.606 --> 01:29:24.025
You gotta be safe for you,
you gotta be safe for her.


01:29:25.318 --> 01:29:29.364
And I promise you I ain't gonna let
a damn thing happen to her.


01:29:32.659 --> 01:29:34.452
- I promise you.
- [sniffles]


01:29:35.912 --> 01:29:37.497
I promise you.


01:29:41.042 --> 01:29:44.045
[suspenseful music playing]


01:29:45.755 --> 01:29:47.382
[sobbing]


01:29:56.850 --> 01:29:58.268
[inhales deeply]


01:30:00.604 --> 01:30:01.855
Just a little bruise.


01:30:19.247 --> 01:30:21.541
[breathing heavily]


01:30:21.625 --> 01:30:25.462
Pull it. Come on, motherfucker.


01:30:25.545 --> 01:30:27.172
[weeping]


01:30:32.469 --> 01:30:35.472
[breathing heavily]


01:30:40.435 --> 01:30:42.687
[exhales sharply]


01:30:45.357 --> 01:30:47.317
You fuckin' pussy.


01:30:53.114 --> 01:30:54.407
Ah...


01:30:57.494 --> 01:30:58.912
It's gonna hurt.


01:31:01.206 --> 01:31:02.999
It's gonna fuckin' hurt.


01:31:07.712 --> 01:31:10.131
[Mitchell] We'll take good care of her,
don't you worry.


01:31:11.633 --> 01:31:13.760
You wanna wake up Analee,


01:31:13.843 --> 01:31:16.012
say goodbye to her before we take off?


01:31:20.058 --> 01:31:21.142
[crying]


01:31:21.226 --> 01:31:24.437
I fuckin' told her I'd never leave her
and here I go, leaving her.


01:31:27.315 --> 01:31:29.609
Every single fuckin' thing
I've done wrong,


01:31:29.693 --> 01:31:32.070
I've brought down on that little girl.


01:31:32.153 --> 01:31:34.489
Hey, life's a whirlwind.
We're all caught up in it.


01:31:35.365 --> 01:31:36.408
You're a good mama.


01:31:37.200 --> 01:31:39.411
Hell, anyone can see
how much you love that little girl,


01:31:39.494 --> 01:31:40.745
you love her so bad, it hurts.


01:31:40.829 --> 01:31:42.831
And if it didn't hurt,
you wouldn't be doing it right.


01:31:44.332 --> 01:31:46.584
That hurt never goes away,
it doesn't matter how old they get.


01:31:49.045 --> 01:31:51.089
Just do the best you can for right now,


01:31:52.382 --> 01:31:54.551
and you don't worry
about tomorrow until it comes.


01:31:59.514 --> 01:32:00.640
You're doing the right thing.


01:32:03.393 --> 01:32:04.394
[sighs]


01:32:08.732 --> 01:32:10.233
- Take care of her.
- Oh, yeah.


01:32:12.610 --> 01:32:15.447
- [Mitchell] Ahem.
- [Maben sobs]


01:32:19.576 --> 01:32:22.579
[suspenseful music playing]


01:32:38.261 --> 01:32:39.554
[exhales sharply]


01:32:42.307 --> 01:32:44.309
[breathing heavily]


01:32:55.612 --> 01:32:58.823
[car doors open and close]


01:33:01.367 --> 01:33:03.369
[footsteps approaching]


01:33:11.503 --> 01:33:12.587
[light switch clicks]


01:33:33.191 --> 01:33:34.400
Coast's clear.


01:33:36.069 --> 01:33:39.114
I've got everything ready here.
Got you a bunch of supplies.


01:33:39.823 --> 01:33:41.616
Can I use your bathroom?


01:33:41.699 --> 01:33:43.034
Sure, down the hall.


01:33:45.662 --> 01:33:47.080
- [Larry yells]
- [crowbar lands]


01:33:48.623 --> 01:33:49.624
Maben!


01:33:50.250 --> 01:33:51.501
[roars]


01:33:51.584 --> 01:33:54.587
- [dramatic music playing]
- [both grunting and groaning]


01:34:03.388 --> 01:34:05.807
- That's all you've got?
- [Russell] Yeah!


01:34:05.890 --> 01:34:09.227
[grunting and groaning continue]


01:34:09.310 --> 01:34:10.645
Motherfucker!


01:34:10.728 --> 01:34:12.021
[grunting]


01:34:20.113 --> 01:34:24.200
You killed the wrong one.
You ain't fucking perfect.


01:34:24.284 --> 01:34:26.244
You should've killed me.


01:34:30.123 --> 01:34:32.584
[Russell breathing heavily]


01:34:34.294 --> 01:34:35.753
It's over now, boy.


01:34:37.547 --> 01:34:38.548
[Russell groans]


01:34:43.678 --> 01:34:46.764
[breathing heavily]


01:34:46.848 --> 01:34:49.726
I've been waitin'
seven fuckin' years for this.


01:34:49.809 --> 01:34:51.019
[gunshot]


01:34:53.354 --> 01:34:54.814
[rifle clatters]


01:34:55.773 --> 01:34:58.109
- [body thuds]
- [Larry groaning]


01:34:58.193 --> 01:34:59.277
You okay, son?


01:35:00.320 --> 01:35:01.654
Dammit, Larry, I'm sorry.


01:35:02.363 --> 01:35:04.782
Why don't you sit down, son?
I'll call you an ambulance.


01:35:04.866 --> 01:35:05.950
[Larry groaning]


01:35:07.452 --> 01:35:08.870
- [shotgun cocks]
- [breathing heavily]


01:35:14.375 --> 01:35:15.460
[Russell] Maben!


01:35:16.294 --> 01:35:17.128
Maben!


01:35:17.879 --> 01:35:19.339
- [shotgun thuds]
- [engine starts]


01:35:19.422 --> 01:35:22.508
Goddammit, Mitchell! I told you
to stay the hell out of this shit.


01:35:22.592 --> 01:35:24.510
- [tires screech]
- You can damn me later.


01:35:24.594 --> 01:35:26.095
We gotta get her the hell outta here.


01:35:27.722 --> 01:35:29.265
[Mitchell] Damn, I knew
he'd do something wrong.


01:35:31.935 --> 01:35:33.937
[grunts] Careful there.


01:35:35.939 --> 01:35:38.483
- Be safe, son.
- [Russell] Get home!


01:35:38.566 --> 01:35:41.194
- Get rid of that fuckin' gun!
- Yeah, yeah.


01:35:41.277 --> 01:35:44.280
[dramatic music playing]


01:35:54.207 --> 01:35:57.210
[extended, insistent honking]


01:36:09.013 --> 01:36:10.098
Come here, boy.


01:36:11.891 --> 01:36:12.892
Cody...


01:36:15.186 --> 01:36:16.479
Cody, boy...


01:36:19.524 --> 01:36:20.566
Cody...


01:36:21.359 --> 01:36:24.570
[yelling] Cody!


01:36:24.654 --> 01:36:28.116
[mumbles indistinct]


01:36:28.199 --> 01:36:29.659
Jesus Christ, Larry...


01:36:31.077 --> 01:36:33.204
- Where is my son?
- Hey, what happened to you?


01:36:33.288 --> 01:36:35.081
- Who did this to you?
- Where is he?


01:36:35.164 --> 01:36:37.166
- Larry...
- Mom, what the fuck's going on?


01:36:37.250 --> 01:36:38.293
- Go call 911!
- Why is he here?


01:36:38.376 --> 01:36:40.003
- Dad, why the fuck are you here?
- Call 911!


01:36:40.086 --> 01:36:42.630
- Why? What's going on?
- [Larry mumbling]


01:36:42.714 --> 01:36:43.881
Is he fuckin' bleeding?


01:36:43.965 --> 01:36:45.758
- Why are you bleeding?
- Go call 911, Cody!


01:36:45.842 --> 01:36:47.677
- He needs help!
- Go call!


01:36:47.760 --> 01:36:50.263
Come here, boy... Let me touch my son.


01:36:51.097 --> 01:36:53.308
[panting] Larry, don't move, please. Okay?


01:36:53.391 --> 01:36:55.601
- Try not to move, Larry...
- Get the fuck away from me.


01:36:55.685 --> 01:36:57.562
- Goddammit. Hey, listen.
- [groaning loudly]


01:36:57.645 --> 01:36:59.480
Stay right there, okay? Don't move!


01:37:00.273 --> 01:37:02.984
- Imma get you help...
- You all did this to me.


01:37:04.610 --> 01:37:07.864
You all did it. You all did it.


01:37:09.407 --> 01:37:10.867
- [dog barking]
- [groaning]


01:37:13.328 --> 01:37:15.163
[breathing heavily]


01:37:20.126 --> 01:37:21.586
[Dana speaking]


01:37:21.669 --> 01:37:23.546
- Hey, you can't go!
- [Cody] Dad, what are you doing?


01:37:23.629 --> 01:37:25.423
- Dad, stop! Where the fuck are you going?
- Hey! You can't...


01:37:25.506 --> 01:37:27.842
You can't drive like that, Larry! Come on!


01:37:28.593 --> 01:37:32.013
Oh, shit, he's driving!
He's driving. He's driving.


01:37:32.096 --> 01:37:33.765
Please hurry!


01:37:33.848 --> 01:37:34.849
Help!


01:37:36.267 --> 01:37:37.852
Somebody help!


01:37:37.935 --> 01:37:40.938
[dramatic music playing]


01:37:43.274 --> 01:37:44.901
Somebody help us!


01:37:48.404 --> 01:37:51.366
Maben... we're here. Maben...


01:37:51.449 --> 01:37:54.285
- [nurse] What happened?
- She... she fell. She...


01:37:54.369 --> 01:37:58.373
hit her head. Her head flipped back.
[mumbles, pants]


01:38:05.213 --> 01:38:08.216
- [dramatic music continues]
- [sirens wailing]


01:38:11.219 --> 01:38:13.638
[yelling]


01:38:17.558 --> 01:38:20.561
[music swells]


01:38:31.030 --> 01:38:34.867
[truck crashes]


01:38:42.875 --> 01:38:44.085
[phones ringing]


01:38:45.628 --> 01:38:47.463
I heard your address on the wire.
Shots fired?


01:38:48.798 --> 01:38:50.383
Hell, yeah, shots fired.


01:38:50.466 --> 01:38:51.676
What the hell happened?


01:38:55.179 --> 01:38:58.766
Walked in my place, Larry was there.


01:38:58.850 --> 01:39:00.893
Had a woman with me,
he hit her over the head


01:39:00.977 --> 01:39:03.271
with a crowbar thinkin' it was me.


01:39:03.354 --> 01:39:04.605
Him and I got into it,


01:39:05.356 --> 01:39:07.817
I got ahold of my rifle and I shot 'im.


01:39:09.193 --> 01:39:10.403
Who is she, Russ?


01:39:12.280 --> 01:39:14.532
You know goddamn well who she is.


01:39:19.954 --> 01:39:22.707
Russ, you gotta tell me.


01:39:22.790 --> 01:39:25.209
What the hell you got to do with all this?


01:39:25.293 --> 01:39:27.295
[woman over P.A. indistinct]


01:39:28.796 --> 01:39:30.840
I'll explain everything to you.


01:39:32.425 --> 01:39:35.470
You gotta promise me you ain't
gonna listen to me like a lawman.


01:39:35.553 --> 01:39:36.762
What do you want me to listen to you like?


01:39:36.846 --> 01:39:39.098
I want you to listen to me
like you're you...


01:39:40.433 --> 01:39:41.684
and I'm me.


01:39:47.857 --> 01:39:49.192
Okay. Okay.


01:39:52.945 --> 01:39:56.866
[indistinct radio chatter]


01:39:59.619 --> 01:40:01.621
[Russell] <i>The pistol you're looking for
is over in the lake.</i>


01:40:02.580 --> 01:40:04.081
<i>Same one Maben held on me</i>


01:40:04.165 --> 01:40:06.542
<i>when I walked out of the Armadillo
a few nights ago.</i>


01:40:07.877 --> 01:40:11.631
<i>That's when she got to talkin'
about how some deputy</i>


01:40:11.714 --> 01:40:14.342
<i>made her do everything
that he wanted her to do,</i>


01:40:14.425 --> 01:40:18.387
<i>even called his goddamned friends along
to come have a go at her too.</i>


01:40:18.471 --> 01:40:21.182
Next thing she knew, he was down, dead,
and she kept on runnin',


01:40:21.265 --> 01:40:23.351
kept on runnin' straight
until she ran into me.


01:40:24.852 --> 01:40:28.064
Why the hell didn't you and her
just both come straight to me?


01:40:29.815 --> 01:40:32.610
Nobody would've believed her
and you know it, Boyd.


01:40:35.613 --> 01:40:37.281
She'da lost the kid.


01:40:37.365 --> 01:40:40.201
And I'll be goddamned,
but I believe everything she says.


01:40:42.954 --> 01:40:44.705
My road's the road
that brought us all here,


01:40:44.789 --> 01:40:46.791
led by what hand, I don't know.


01:40:46.874 --> 01:40:49.085
But here we are,
and I ain't lettin' this go.


01:40:50.127 --> 01:40:51.546
Shit, I'm only telling you all this


01:40:51.629 --> 01:40:54.090
so you know when I ask you,
just leave her alone.


01:40:54.173 --> 01:40:56.092
I ain't tellin' you, I'm askin' you.


01:40:58.886 --> 01:41:00.388
Just let it fall.


01:41:01.722 --> 01:41:02.890
Let it fall?


01:41:04.767 --> 01:41:05.935
Just let it fall.


01:41:07.687 --> 01:41:09.522
Do you know who's at my house right now?


01:41:12.358 --> 01:41:13.609
Yes, I do.


01:41:13.693 --> 01:41:16.946
And do you know what the boys at Parchman
would do to a sheriff's deputy?


01:41:17.029 --> 01:41:19.323
Huh? It'd make your time
look like summer camp.


01:41:27.957 --> 01:41:29.500
Where's the proof, Russell?


01:41:38.551 --> 01:41:40.177
[vehicle approaching]


01:41:50.688 --> 01:41:51.814
[casings clink]


01:41:51.897 --> 01:41:54.025
[dramatic music playing]


01:42:04.368 --> 01:42:05.369
[whistles]


01:42:13.336 --> 01:42:14.545
What does that look like to you?


01:42:18.174 --> 01:42:21.177
[music swells]


01:42:51.207 --> 01:42:54.210
[pensive music playing]


01:42:59.423 --> 01:43:00.841
[muted dialogue]


01:43:16.065 --> 01:43:17.400
[Maben] <i>The days are slow.</i>


01:43:19.402 --> 01:43:21.987
<i>They get that way when you're waiting
on something to happen</i>


01:43:22.071 --> 01:43:23.572
<i>that you hope never will.</i>


01:43:28.786 --> 01:43:31.414
<i>You can't help but wonder
if today is the day...</i>


01:43:33.416 --> 01:43:34.709
<i>they'll be sittin' there,</i>


01:43:35.626 --> 01:43:38.587
<i>that here they come, over that hill,</i>


01:43:38.671 --> 01:43:41.882
<i>down the driveway, lights flashing,</i>


01:43:43.008 --> 01:43:44.802
<i>sirens calling out your name.</i>


01:43:47.304 --> 01:43:49.181
<i>Russell told me about this dream</i>


01:43:49.265 --> 01:43:51.434
<i>of being back on the inside,</i>


01:43:52.435 --> 01:43:54.562
<i>about how the light was always grey,</i>


01:43:56.105 --> 01:43:58.482
<i>and there was always
this voice calling out...</i>


01:44:00.818 --> 01:44:02.445
<i>Just some cry,</i>


01:44:02.528 --> 01:44:04.363
<i>echoing through an empty prison...</i>


01:44:07.616 --> 01:44:09.910
<i>and he never knew
what he was supposed to do.</i>


01:44:11.829 --> 01:44:14.165
<i>If he was supposed to be helping it, or...</i>


01:44:15.708 --> 01:44:17.460
<i>if it was there to help him.</i>


01:44:20.713 --> 01:44:22.173
[Analee giggles]


01:44:22.256 --> 01:44:24.341
[Mabel speaks indistinctly]


01:44:24.425 --> 01:44:25.593
[Analee screams]


01:44:25.676 --> 01:44:27.970
<i>Sometimes I think it was me
he was hearing...</i>


01:44:30.806 --> 01:44:33.809
[soft music continues]


01:44:39.648 --> 01:44:42.485
<i>I don't guess there's no way
of knowing what's coming.</i>


01:44:46.113 --> 01:44:49.366
<i>Never has been. Never will be.</i>


01:44:52.453 --> 01:44:53.579
<i>But, for once,</i>


01:44:55.080 --> 01:44:56.248
<i>I'm not afraid.</i>


01:45:09.887 --> 01:45:11.096
[Analee giggling]


01:45:19.605 --> 01:45:22.525
- [laughing]
- [muted dialogue]


01:45:22.608 --> 01:45:24.610
[birds chirping]


01:45:28.155 --> 01:45:29.990
<i>And when the daylight fades,</i>


01:45:32.284 --> 01:45:34.370
<i>and it seems okay to breathe a little...</i>


01:45:39.208 --> 01:45:40.709
<i>that low light</i>


01:45:41.752 --> 01:45:43.671
<i>gives her this long shadow,</i>


01:45:44.421 --> 01:45:46.340
<i>like her arms are spread out.</i>


01:45:48.592 --> 01:45:50.219
<i>As if she's saying,</i>


01:45:50.302 --> 01:45:53.305
<i>"Come here and let me hold you..."</i>


01:45:53.389 --> 01:45:56.225
[indistinct chatter]


01:45:57.434 --> 01:45:58.602
<i>I don't know...</i>


01:45:58.686 --> 01:46:01.897
- [laughing]
- Get... get up! Get up! Here, stand up.


01:46:01.981 --> 01:46:03.899
<i>Maybe there is such a thing as a miracle.</i>


01:46:04.775 --> 01:46:06.777
I got you! [laughs]


01:46:18.247 --> 01:46:19.915
<i>All I know for certain...</i>


01:46:23.919 --> 01:46:25.045
<i>she's mine.</i>


01:46:33.262 --> 01:46:34.346
[music ends]


01:46:37.850 --> 01:46:39.852
["Desperation Road"
by Garrett Hedlund begins]


01:46:48.277 --> 01:46:51.280
[song continues]


01:48:58.615 --> 01:49:01.618
[song ends]


01:49:04.413 --> 01:49:07.207
["Wolves" by Sanders Bohlke begins]


01:50:10.729 --> 01:50:13.732
[song continues]


01:51:56.710 --> 01:51:58.086
[song ends]

